window.EB_SB_ADD({"hells-destiny-bestiary/advodaza":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","telepathy 100 feet"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"focus":3,"flavor":"<p>These devils prey upon the superstitious, masquerading as lost or obscure divinities, and ultimately corrupt whatever cults they rule.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"At-Will Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster can cast its at-will spells any number of times without using up spell slots.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Idol Armor","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The advodaza's defiled idols grant them resistance 15 to two damage types of their choice except fire, physical, poison, and spirit (typically mental and void). The advodaza can spend 10 minutes to change which damage types are resisted. Any holy effect that affects the fiend can also counteract their idol armor (DC 40), which the advodaza can reactivate with a Sustain action.</p>"},{"n":"False Divinity","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The advodaza chooses two domains, typically chosen from the following list: ambition, darkness, fire, might, trickery, tyranny, wealth, or zeal. The advodaza gains both domains' initial domain spells as well as the advanced domain spell from one of the domains, all heightened to 9th rank.</p><hr><p><em>Note: For the purposes of Foundry Data Entry, fire and might were the domains chosen. Change the focus spells the Advodaza knows for the domains of your choice.</em></p>"},{"n":"Infernal Mark","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The advodaza touches a willing creature and marks it with a glyph that functions as a 9th-rank Sigil, which the devil can make visible or invisible. The target gains 1 Focus Point if it didn't already have any, and the advodaza grants it one of their initial domain spells as a focus spell. The marked creature and the advodaza can communicate telepathically with each other while on the same plane. The advodaza can maintain up to 10 Infernal Marks at a time; if they create another after reaching this limit, the oldest mark is Dismissed. The advodaza can Dismiss any number of Infernal Marks with a single action.</p>"},{"n":"Punish Disciple","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["spirit"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The advodaza chooses up to three creatures bearing their Infernal Mark that are on the same plane as the advodaza, dealing 8d6 spirit damage to each creature (DC 40 basic Fortitude save).</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/alcabanoth":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","telepathy 100 feet"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"focus":3,"flavor":"<p>These devils prey upon the superstitious, masquerading as lost or obscure divinities, and ultimately corrupt whatever cults they rule.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"At-Will Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster can cast its at-will spells any number of times without using up spell slots.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Idol Armor","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The advodaza's defiled idols grant them resistance 15 to two damage types of their choice except fire, physical, poison, and spirit (typically mental and void). The advodaza can spend 10 minutes to change which damage types are resisted. Any holy effect that affects the fiend can also counteract their idol armor (DC 40), which the advodaza can reactivate with a Sustain action.</p>"},{"n":"False Divinity","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Alcabanoth has access to the ambition and zeal domains.</p><hr><p>The advodaza chooses two domains, typically chosen from the following list: ambition, darkness, fire, might, trickery, tyranny, wealth, or zeal. The advodaza gains both domains' initial domain spells as well as the advanced domain spell from one of the domains, all heightened to 9th rank.</p>"},{"n":"Infernal Mark","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The advodaza touches a willing creature and marks it with a glyph that functions as a 9th-rank Sigil, which the devil can make visible or invisible. The target gains 1 Focus Point if it didn't already have any, and the advodaza grants it one of their initial domain spells as a focus spell. The marked creature and the advodaza can communicate telepathically with each other while on the same plane. The advodaza can maintain up to 10 Infernal Marks at a time; if they create another after reaching this limit, the oldest mark is Dismissed. The advodaza can Dismiss any number of Infernal Marks with a single action.</p>"},{"n":"Punish Disciple","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["spirit"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The advodaza chooses up to three creatures bearing their Infernal Mark that are on the same plane as the advodaza, dealing 8d6 spirit damage to each creature (DC 40 basic Fortitude save).</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/alchemical-cloud":{"description":"<p>The collection of bottles at the bottom of one locker have been jostled. Their contents leak into a puddle, and their vapors burn through the open air.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 30 Crafting (master) to neutralize the alchemical substances, or DC 35 Thievery (expert) to carefully clean the spill</p>","reset":"<p>If the reagents aren't cleaned up before closing the locker, the accumulating gases reset the trap after 1 hour.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Leaking Reagents","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["inhaled","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature fully opens the locker containing the alchemical clutter</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> A cloud of vapor deals 8d10 poison damage to all creatures within 10 feet (DC 36 basic Reflex save). On a failure, a target takes an additional 2d10 persistent poison damage.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/angelic-host":{"lang":["Diabolic","Draconic","Empyrean","truespeech"],"notes":{"speed":"troop movement"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Aura of Righteousness","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet. Allies in the angelic host's aura gain a +2 status bonus to AC and saving throws against unholy creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Blessed Armaments","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["holy","magical"],"f":"","d":"<p>The angels make coordinated melee attacks with their greatswords. Each enemy within a 5-foot emanation must attempt a DC 39 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 2d8 slashing plus 1d6 spirit damage</p>\n<p>2 4d8+8 slashing plus 2d6 spirit damage</p>\n<p>3 6d8+10 slashing plus 3d6 spirit damage</p>"},{"n":"Divine Lance Fusillade","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["holy","magical"],"f":"","d":"<p>The angels unleash beams of divine energy in a 10-foot burst within 60 feet that deals 10d6 spirit damage with a DC 39 basic Reflex save. When the angelic host is reduced to 2 segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Troop Spellcasting","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the angelic host Casts a healing Spell, the constituent members combine their efforts into casting a more powerful version of the spell than any one member could achieve alone. The spell restores an additional 2 Hit Points per rank.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/anguished-hellfire":{"lang":["Diabolic","Pyric","truespeech"],"lore":[["Asmodeus Lore",33]],"abilities":[{"n":"Eternal Luminosity","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["light"],"f":"","d":"<p>An anguished hellfire naturally sheds brilliant light like a torch. When other creatures target the anguished hellfire, they ignore the Concealed condition from darkness, fog, mist, and smoke.</p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Solar Flare","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. When a creature ends its turn in the aura, it takes 4d6 fire damage (DC 38 basic Fortitude save). On a failed save, it also becomes Dazzled until the end of its next turn. The anguished hellfire can deactivate or activate this aura by using a single action that has the concentrate trait.</p>"},{"n":"Vulnerable to Blasphemy","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If a creature the anguished flame can see and hear spends 1 action with the linguistic trait blaspheming Asmodeus, the anguished flame becomes Sickened 1 until they Collect a Prayer from that creature.</p>"},{"n":"Collect Unholy Prayer","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The anguished flame compels the prayers of a creature they can see within 60 feet, and that creature must attempt a DC 41 Will save. A creature with the holy trait gets a degree of success one better than their result.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature uses its reaction to pray.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature prays. It is Slowed 1 and can't use reactions for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature is Slowed 2.</p>"},{"n":"Focus Gaze","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The anguished hellfire's solar flare aura is active</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The anguished hellfire fixes their fiery eyes on a creature they can see within 30 feet. The target must immediately attempt a Fortitude save against the anguished hellfire's solar flare. If the creature was already Dazzled by solar flare before attempting its save, a failed save causes it to become Blinded until the end of its next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Scourging Flame","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hellfire can burn away beneficial magic. It attempts a flaming wing Strike. On a success, the anguished hellfire attempts to counteract one spell effect of its choice active on the target. The counteract modifier is +36, and the counteract rank is 9th.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/animated-cage-trap":{"description":"<p>A spiky iron cage pulls in a victim with animated chains before slamming shut and locking tight.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 45 Thievery (master) to Pick the Lock, DC 48 Athletics (master) to break the lock or bend the bars; five total successes are required to disable the trap</p>","reset":"<p>The trap deactivates 1 minute after there are no longer any potential prisoners in the room and then activates 1 round after that.</p>","routine":"<p>(3 actions) As 1 action, the trap makes a chain Strike against a target in its reach; its Athletics modifier for Improved Grab is +36. The trap can have any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by its chains. If the trap has any creatures grabbed or restrained, it attempts to pull them closer as 1 action with an Athletics check against the creature's Fortitude DC; on a success, it pulls the creature 5 feet closer (10 feet on a critical success). A Large or smaller creature can be pulled inside the cage, after which the cage door slams shut. The cage can only contain one creature, and that creature is restrained while inside (Escape). As 1 action, the trap can Constrict the creature inside the cage with more chains.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master) <br></p>","abilities":[{"n":"Capturing Chain","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature that isn't a member of the inquisition or an authorized ally comes within 15 feet of the cage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The trap makes a chain Strike against the triggering creature. If the trap damages and successfully grapples the target with Improved Grab, the trap pulls the target 5 feet closer (or into the cage if the Strike was a critical hit). The trap then rolls initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>3d8+20 bludgeoning, DC 45 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC.</p></p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/aquatic-viper-vine":{"flavor":"<p>A voracious, flesh-eating carnivore, the viper vine has a single enormous blossom arising from a thick, leafy tangle of snakelike vines. When the plant senses the approach of suitable prey through its sensitive, shallow-buried root system, it rises up like an agitated snake and unfurls its brightly colored bloom, an act that releases a cloud of mind-numbing pollen.</p>\n<p>Since viper vines gain nourishment by consuming creatures rather than through photosynthesis and absorbing nutrients from the soil, they have developed rudimentary locomotion and can drag themselves along the ground with tentacle-like roots. They even have a form of rudimentary sentience, allowing them to both discern differences in prey and make limited tactical decisions, while also avoiding creatures that are particularly large or dangerous looking.</p>\n<p>The area around viper vine hunting grounds is often strewn with the partially devoured remains of victims. It's not unusual to find the rotting corpses of wild animals, ill-fated adventurers, and even giants in the plant's immediate vicinity, along with a scattering of incidental treasure left behind on the corpses. A viper vine rarely returns to the carcass of a creature it killed earlier, preferring to hunt fresh meat.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Tremorsense 60 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Tremorsense allows a monster to feel the vibrations through a solid surface caused by movement. It is an imprecise sense with a limited range (listed in the ability). Tremorsense functions only if the monster is on the same surface as the subject, and only if the subject is moving along (or burrowing through) the surface.</p></p>"},{"n":"Cold Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["cold"],"f":"","d":"<p>When exposed to a cold effect, the viper vine is overwhelmed by lethargy, becoming Slowed 1 for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Captivating Pollen","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["incapacitation","mental","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>The viper vine releases a 60-foot emanation of invisible pollen that stays in the air for 5 rounds unless dispersed by a moderate or stronger wind. Each creature that enters or starts its turn in the area must succeed at a DC 33 Will save or be captivated.</p>\n<p>The viper vine can't use Captivating Pollen for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Captivating Pollen for 24 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Sickened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Fascinated, and it must spend each of its actions to move closer to the viper vine as expediently as possible while avoiding obvious dangers. If a captivated creature is adjacent to the viper vine, it stays still and doesn't act. It ceases to be fascinated if it's no longer in the pollen aura at the end of its turn.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, plus the creature is Stupefied 2 for 24 hours.</p>"},{"n":"Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>3d8+8 bludgeoning damage, DC 33 basic Fortitude</p>\n<hr>\n<p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC.</p></p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/archheathens-fool":{"notes":{"ac":"(34 when broken)"},"abilities":[{"n":"Construct Armor (Hardness 10)","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Like normal objects, the archheathen's fool has Hardness. This Hardness reduces any damage it takes by an amount equal to the Hardness. Once the archheathen's fool is reduced to less than half its Hit Points, or immediately upon being damaged by a critical hit, its construct armor breaks, removing the Hardness and reducing its Armor Class to 34.</p>"},{"n":"Trickery Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The effigy is easily tricked. It isn't immune to attempts to Create a diversion or Feint. If a creature succeeds at either action, it becomes Slowed 1 for 1 round as it processes the trickery. Each additional success increases its slowed condition by 1.</p>"},{"n":"Push","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Push in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Shove the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty. If Push lists a distance, change the distance the creature is pushed on a success to that distance.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/aspexia-rugatonn":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Empyrean"],"lore":[["Hell Lore",35]],"gear":["Mace","Breastplate","Key"],"focus":2,"abilities":[{"n":"Cast Down in Flames","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","spellshape"],"f":"","d":"<p>Aspexia brings the sheer force of her faith crashing down on a foe. If the next action she takes is to cast Harm to damage one creature, the target is knocked Prone if it takes any damage from the spell. If the target fails its saving throw against the spell, it also takes 3d6 persistent fire damage.</p>"},{"n":"Channel Smite","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Aspexia expends a Harm spell</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Aspexia makes a melee Strike. If it hits, she damages the target with a 1-action <em>harm</em> spell, The target automatically gets a failure (or a critical failure if the Strike was a critical hit). The spell doesn't have the manipulate trait when cast this way.</p>"},{"n":"Deadly Simplicity","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Aspexia deals 1d8 damage with her mace instead of 1d6.</p>"},{"n":"Rebounding Smite","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Aspexia misses with her Strike during Channel Smite</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Aspexia retains the energy from her smite. She Casts the 1-action version of the Harm spell she expended, targeting a creature other than the target of her Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Unholy Bloodshed","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Aspexia critically succeeds at an attack roll against a holy creature with her Unholy Mace</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The target takes 3d8 bleed.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/athervox":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Elven","Empyrean","Fey","Jotun"],"lore":[["Astronomy Lore",32]],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. primal","speed":"forest passage, trackless journey"},"abilities":[{"n":"Camouflage","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Athervox can Hide in natural environments even if she doesn't have cover.</p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Primal","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Frightful Presence","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>90 feet. DC 39 Will</p><hr><p><p>A creature that first enters the area must attempt a Will save.</p>\n<p>Regardless of the result of the saving throw, the creature is temporarily immune to this monster's Frightful Presence for 1 minute.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected by the presence.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 4.</p></p>"},{"n":"Miasma","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet. After Athervox uses her Poison Breath, a cloud of poison gas continues to emanate from her body for 1 round. Any creature that ends their turn in the miasma takes 4d6 poison damage (DC 39 basic Fortitude save). Any creature in the miasma is Concealed and treats other creatures as concealed. Athervox can see through this concealment.</p>\n<p>Effect: Miasma</p>"},{"n":"Thrusting Tail","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within reach of Athervox's tail Casts a Spell</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Athervox makes a tail Strike at the creature with a –2 penalty. If the Strike hits, Athervox disrupts the creature's action.</p>"},{"n":"Warding Focus","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Spells that Athervox Casts that target herself have their durations doubled.</p>"},{"n":"Forest Passage","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Athervox ignores all difficult terrain caused by plants, such as bushes, vines, and undergrowth. Even plants manipulated by magic doesn't impede her progress.</p>"},{"n":"Impaling Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Athervox doesn't have a creature impaled on her horn</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Athervox attempts to gore a foe. She Strides, then attempts a horn Strike. On a hit, the target becomes impaled on Athervox's horn. The creature is Grabbed while on the horn (and can Escape as normal). Athervox doesn't need to use additional actions to keep the impaled creature grabbed. If Athervox moves, she brings the grabbed creature along with her.</p>"},{"n":"Poison Breath","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Athervox breathes a toxic cloud that deals 19d6 poison damage in a 60-foot cone (DC 39 basic Fortitude save) that doesn't damage objects. She can't use Poison Breath again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Telescopic Scrying","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":["primal","scrying"],"f":"once per hour","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> When peering through a telescope, Athervox can survey and monitor her surroundings as well as astronomical phenomena. She can cast Alarm and Scouting Eye, each with a maximum range of 5 miles from the telescope used as a focus.</p>"},{"n":"Trackless Journey","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Athervox always gains the benefit of Cover Tracks in natural surroundings, even while moving at full speed.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/avernal-vortex":{"description":"<p>The edges of the extraplanar tunnel seem to writhe with malevolence, as if preventing unwanted souls from passing through.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 50 Arcana (master) or DC 50 Religion (master) to allow the group to traverse along the portal tunnel; six total successes are required to complete the journey; a PC who succeeds at a DC 48 Acrobatics, DC 48 Athletics, or DC 48 Survival check as a 2-action activity grants themselves a +2 circumstance bonus to AC and saves against the hazard's routine for 1 round (on a critical success, they can also grant this bonus to one other PC)</p>","reset":"<p>Once the PCs pass through the portal tunnel and arrive in Hell, the Avernal vortex ends and doesn't reset.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action; divine) The Avernal vortex churns across the portal tunnel, stopping the PCs from reaching their ultimate destination. In the first round, the vortex takes an action to attempt to dispel all beneficial spells on all creatures in the tunnel, scouring them with Hellfire. The vortex has a counteract modifier of +43 and a counteract rank of 10, and rolls separately for each spell. On a success, the target creature takes 4d6 fire damage with a DC 45 basic Fortitude save (this has the divine, fire, and unholy traits).</p><p>In the second round, the vortex attempts to instill a dread of tumbling forever through the tunnel to those within it; each creature takes 6d6 persistent mental damage with a DC 45 basic Will save (this is an emotion and mental effect). Once a creature ends its persistent mental damage (or if they avoided the persistent damage), they can reach and escape the tunnel.</p><p>In all subsequent rounds, the vortex releases bolts of acid, cold, fire, and electricity. It makes one vortex bolt Strike against each creature in the tunnel.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(legendary)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Gaze of Barbatos","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["divine","emotion","fear","fire","mental","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A living creature enters the portal tunnel</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> As the PCs begin to pierce planar boundaries, they feel they've caught the attention of the archdevil Barbatos, ruler of Avernus. Each creature in the tunnel must attempt a DC 45 Will save. The hazard then rolls initiative.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Stupefied 1 for 1 round and Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Stupefied 2 for 1 minute and Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Stupefied 3 for 1 minute and Frightened 3.</p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Vortex Bolt":"<p>acid, cold, fire, or electricity; the damage is chosen randomly, and the Strike gains the appropriate trait; no multiple attack penalty</p>"}},"hells-destiny-bestiary/bdellavritra":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Empyrean","telepathy 100 feet, truespeech"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"flavor":"<p>Masters of possession, bdellavritras enact complex schemes through pawns in the mortal world. Even if expelled from their hosts, these fiends retain fearsome physical strength with bodies that bely their agility.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"At-Will Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster can cast its at-will spells any number of times without using up spell slots.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>3d8+6 bludgeoning, DC 34 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC.</p></p>"},{"n":"Mental Synergy","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","spellshape"],"f":"once per minute","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per minute</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The bdellavritra is possessing a host using Mind Worm</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If the bdellavritra's next action is to Cast a Spell, they reduce the number of actions to cast it by 1 (minimum 1 action).</p>"},{"n":"Mind Worm","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","incapacitation","mental","possession"],"f":"","d":"<p>The bdellavritra spends 10 minutes adjacent to an Unconscious or willing living creature, then attempts to possess its body. This functions as Possession heightened to 9th rank (DC 37 Will save), except that it has a duration of 1 month. If affected, the host receives new saving throws only at the start of each day. If the host dies, the bdellavritra must attempt a Fortitude save as normal but is only Stunned 2 on a failure (or Stunned 4 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Pleasant Voices","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate","emotion","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The bdellavritra isn't possessing a host</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> One of the bdellavritra's mouths sings to a living creature within 30 feet. Unless the target succeeds at a DC 37 Will save (with a +4 circumstance bonus if the devil or their allies recently threatened the target), they can't use hostile actions against the bdellavritra for 1 round. The bdellavritra can Sustain this effect for up to 1 hour; each time they do, they can affect an additional target (maximum four targets). Each affected target can attempt a new saving throw to end the effect whenever they can't hear the bdellavritra for 1 round or the devil uses a hostile action against one of them.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/bellflower-chant":{"description":"<p>A chorus of Bellflower Network agents and allies chant about freedom from tyranny.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 21 Performance (trained) to join the chant, or DC 25 Society to identify the Bellflower agents' tactics</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action) The Bellflower chant continues their song. All non–Bellflower Network creatures in area A must attempt a DC 26 Will save. On a failure, the target is offguard until the end of its next turn.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Find Freedom in the Song","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","linguistic","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Zefiro becomes Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The Bellflower chant swells from the assembled crowd. All grabbed, restrained, or Immobilized creatures can attempt to Escape as a free action. The Bellflower chant then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/brimstone-corps":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Warfare Lore",24]],"notes":{"speed":"troop movement"},"flavor":"<p>Soldiers who participate in multiple campaigns of war gain the experience necessary to become their military's finest fighting forces. First-class infantry troops are deployed on battlefields where winning the day is of the utmost importance.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Hell's Call","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Brimstone Corps have pledged their souls to Hell and welcome its embrace. The troop doesn't attempt a rout check when it's reduced from one HP threshold to another. When reduced to 2 segments, the troop gains a +2 circumstance bonus to attack and damage rolls as the last surviving troop members sell their lives dearly before they're called to Hell.</p>"},{"n":"No Retreat","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>These soldiers have been extensively trained to hold their ground no matter the situation. If any effect would force the brimstone corps to move, reduce the distance by 10 feet. Any time they would be affected by the Fleeing condition, the brimstone corps is instead Slowed 2 for the same duration.</p>"},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>HP</strong> 240 (4 segments); <strong>Thresholds</strong> 160 (3 segments), 80 (2 segments)</p>\n<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Bolt Salvo","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The brimstone corps draws, loads, and shoots a salvo from their crossbows. The salvo is a 10-foot burst within 120 feet that deals 4d8 piercing damage (DC 30 basic Reflex save). When the brimstone corps is reduced to 2 segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Clash of Steel","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p>1 to 3</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The brimstone corps attacks each enemy in a 5-foot emanation, with a DC 29 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 2d6+1 slashing damage</p>\n<p>2 4d6+10 slashing damage</p>\n<p>3 4d6+18 slashing damage</p>"},{"n":"Drilled in Formations","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The brimstone corps uses Change Formation. A brimstone corps unit typically knows the marching column and wedge formations.</p>"},{"n":"First-class Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The brimstone corps rushes forward with a hunger for battle. They Stride up to twice their Speed. At the end of their movement, each enemy within a 5-foot emanation takes 2d6+5 slashing damage, with a DC 30 basic Reflex save.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/captivating-gem":{"description":"<p>The floating gem flares with inner radiance, sending out beams of light to captivate and drain the vitality from all who approach.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 35 Arcana (expert), DC 35 Occultism (expert), or DC 35 Religion (expert) to unravel the magical matrix within the gem, DC 40 Crafting or DC 40 Thievery check to unbalance the crystal's alignment, or a DC 43 Athletics check to damage one of the gem's facets and change its geometry; two successes are required to disable the hazard</p>","routine":"<p>(3 actions) The captivating gem attempts uses all three of its actions to incapacitate creatures. It targets the closest creature with its Freezing Light ability, then a different creature with its facet flare Strike. If a creature has already been Paralyzed by Freezing Light, it chooses a different target for that ability.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Freezing Light","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["force","nonlethal","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The captivating gem shines intense light on a living creature, freezing it in place. The target must attempt a DC 40 Fortitude Save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is Stunned 1 and takes 2d12 force damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is Paralyzed for 1 round and takes 4d12 force damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target is paralyzed for 1 round and takes 8d12 force damage.</p>"},{"n":"Glint","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Any living creature approaches within 10 feet of the gem</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The captivating gem targets the triggering creature with a facet flare Strike and then rolls initiative.</p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Facet Flare":"<p>The target must succeed at a DC 40 Fortitude save or become Drained 1</p>"}},"hells-destiny-bestiary/cathilias-meddling":{"description":"<p>A Hellknight on horseback shouts commands, beseeching all to return to order.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 21 Hellknight Lore (trained) to convince the Hellknight that she's adding to chaos, or DC 25 Diplomacy to request she stop yelling</p>","routine":"<p>(3 actions) Cathilia uses her Hellknight's Orders Strike on creatures engaged in open fighting in area <strong>A2</strong>. She randomly chooses between targets in the likely case that there are multiple combatants.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Stop, Burglar","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","linguistic","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature other than Zefiro opens the Museum's gates</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Cathilia shouts at the triggering creature. The target must succeed at a DC 27 Will save or have their action disrupted, and then Cathilia's meddling rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/champion-of-asmodeus":{"lang":["Common","Empyrean"],"gear":["Crossbow","Longsword","Steel Shield","Full Plate","Religious Symbol of Asmodeus","Potion of Flying (Standard)","Viper's Fang","Bolts (20)"],"focus":2,"flavor":"<p>The deific champion is the paragon of champions, representing the truest form of devotion and dedication to a deity.</p><hr><p>Religions inspire devout individuals to uphold their tenets.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Blessed Shield","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>In the deific champion's hands, a shield gains the <em>moderate reinforcing rune</em>, giving it Hardness 8, 84 HP, and BT 42.</p>"},{"n":"Deific Reactions","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>At the start of each of their turns, the deific champion gains an additional reaction they can only use to make a Reactive Strike or to Shield Block.</p>"},{"n":"Champion's Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>15 feet. Any follower of Asmodeus in the aura knows the champion is a champion of Asmodeus. Enemies in the champion's aura take a –1 circumstance penalty to saving throws against fear. In addition, an enemy that ends its turn in the champion's aura can't reduce the value of its frightened condition below 1.</p>"},{"n":"Champion's Courage","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the champion becomes Frightened, they reduce the condition value by 1 (to a minimum of 0).</p>"},{"n":"Exalted Retributive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy damages the deific champion's ally, and both are in the deific champion's aura</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ally gains resistance 14 to all damage against the triggering damage. If the enemy is within reach, the deific champion makes a melee Strike against it. Each ally in the champion's aura can spend a reaction to Strike the target with a –5 penalty.</p>\n<p>Effect: Exalted Retributive Strike</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Will Not Fall","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The deific champion's Hit Points are reduced to 0 for the first time that day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The champion presses on, refusing to fail their god. They remain standing with 25 Hit Points.</p>"},{"n":"Will Not Falter","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Effect</strong> The deific champion declares their devotion to their deity and their cause. They Stride, then make a melee Strike. If the Strike hits an enemy, all allies within their champion's aura gain a +2 status bonus to attack rolls and saving throws against fear until the start of the deific champion's next turn.</p>\n<p>Effect: Will Not Falter</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/collapsing-egorian-building":{"description":"<p>Tremors from the changing landscape could cause a building to collapse.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 45 Athletics (master), DC 45 Crafting (master), or DC 45 Engineering lore (master) to brace the structure against collapse until the end of the creature's next turn. The DC of the flat check for this round (see Routine) decreases by 4 on a success (or by 8 on a critical success). Decreasing the flat check DC to 0 stabilizes the structure, ending this hazard.</p>","reset":"<p>The building becomes susceptible to Shake to Pieces again 1d4 rounds after it's stabilized.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action) The GM rolls a DC 11 Flat, decreasing the DC as noted above. If the check fails, dust and debris fall within the building and 30 feet around it, providing concealment for 1 round and dealing 10d6 bludgeoning damage to 1d4 randomly chosen targets in the area (DC 40 basic Reflex save); a target that critically fails this save is also knocked Prone. If the flat check critically fails, the effect is the same, but damage from the debris increases to 16d6, it affects 2d4 randomly chosen targets, and a creature that critically fails its save is knocked prone and Restrained by the rubble (Escape, Force open).</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert) to notice cracks forming in the walls of the structure</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Shake to Pieces","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The Hellfire tornado moves adjacent to the building</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The building trembles. The floors of the building and the streets within 30 feet of the building become difficult terrain; creatures on this difficult terrain take a –2 circumstance penalty to attack rolls, AC, and skill checks. The hazard rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/crowncrusher-bulwark":{"flavor":"<p>Stone bulwarks are slow and steady constructs typically carved from marble or granite. They're often made to serve as works of art when at rest, so some magical crafters employ master sculptors to ensure their constructs make beautiful statues. Older stone bulwarks might be weathered, with scuffed or cracked surfaces or missing noses and digits, but this weathering is largely cosmetic and doesn't adversely impact the bulwark's functionality.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Statuary Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["arcane","aura","earth"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet.</p>\n<p>Rocks of marble magically arise from the ground in the aura. They protect the bulwark's allies, giving each of them standard Cover. These stones can be used for Throw Rock.</p>\n<p>This aura automatically activates at the start of the stone bulwark's first turn in combat and deactivates at the end of combat.</p>"},{"n":"Binding Stone","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["arcane","earth"],"f":"","d":"<p>Any creature hit by the stone bulwark's fist or rock Strike is affected by a DC 30 Fortitude Earthbind spell.</p>"},{"n":"Inexorable March","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The stone bulwark Strides up to its Speed, pushing back each creature whose space it moves into and damaging them if they try to stop its movement. A creature can attempt to bar the way by succeeding at a DC 34 Fortitude save. On a critical success, the resisting creature takes no damage; otherwise it is damaged as if hit by the construct's fist.</p>"},{"n":"Throw Rock","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster picks up a rock within reach or retrieves a stowed rock and throws it, making a ranged Strike.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/crowncrusher-riot":{"description":"<p>A crew of anarchists rush to fight the dottari.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 21 Intimidation to force them to back down, or DC 25 Diplomacy (expert) to request that they only injure the dottari</p>","routine":"<p>(2 actions) The rioters lob bricks and other heavy objects at any dottari excruciator divisions as an action, dealing 2d6+10 bludgeoning damage to the dottari and any adjacent creatures (DC 27 basic Reflex save).</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"While They're Distracted","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["fire"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A dottari excruciator division deals damage to a living creature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The Crowncrusher riot throws a volley of homemade explosives that deals 2d10 fire damage to the triggering creature and all creatures within 10 feet of it (DC 27 basic Reflex save), and then rolls initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Languages","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Common</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/cultist-of-torment":{"lang":["Alghollthu","Azlanti","Common"],"gear":["Trident"],"abilities":[{"n":"Alleviation Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever an effect restores at least one foe within 30 feet of the cultist to the target's full Hit Points, the cultist takes 2d8 mental damage.</p>"},{"n":"Amplify Torment","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The cultist's Strikes deal an additional 1d8 mental damage to creatures that are injured. This additional damage increases to 1d12 mental if the target has fewer than half its HP remaining.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/daidian-ruel":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Necril"],"lore":[["Hell Lore",36],["Warfare Lore",36]],"gear":["Mace","Sturdy Shield (Major)","Hellknight Plate"],"notes":{"hp":"rejuvenation, void healing","ac":" (46 with shield raised)"},"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Rejuvenation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a graveknight is destroyed, their armor rebuilds their body over the course of 1d10 days—or more quickly if the armor is worn by a living host. If the body is destroyed before then, the process restarts.</p>\n<p>A graveknight can only be permanently destroyed by obliterating their armor (such as with Disintegrate), transporting it to the Forge of Creation, or throwing it into the heart of a volcano.</p>"},{"n":"Sacrilegious Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet.</p>\n<p>When a creature in the aura uses a vitality spell or ability, the graveknight automatically attempts to counteract it, with a counteract modifier of +34.</p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Devastating Blast","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane"],"f":"","d":"<p>The graveknight unleashes a 30-foot cone of energy. Creatures in the area take 21d6 mental with a DC 40 basic Will save.</p>\n<p>The graveknight can use this ability once every 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Graveknight's Curse","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["arcane","curse"],"f":"","d":"<p>This curse affects anyone who wears a graveknight's armor for at least 1 hour</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 42 Will save</p>\n<p><strong>Onset</strong> 1 hour</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Doomed 1 and can't remove armor (1 day)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Doomed 2, –10-foot status penalty to Speeds, and can't remove armor (1 day)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> dies and transforms into the armor's graveknight.</p>"},{"n":"Phantom Mount","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","summon"],"f":"","d":"<p>HP 125; AC 40, Fort +32, Ref +27, Will +29</p><hr><p>The graveknight summons a supernatural mount, as Marvelous Mount heightened to a rank equal to half the graveknight's level. Unlike <em>marvelous mount</em>, the steed's AC and saving throw bonuses are all 4 lower than the graveknight's, and the steed has one-third the graveknight's Hit Points (rounded down).</p>\n<p>If the steed is destroyed, the graveknight must wait 1 hour before using this ability again.</p>"},{"n":"Ruinous Weapons","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Any weapon the graveknight wields or unarmed attack the graveknight uses gains the effects of the <em>greater fearsome</em> weapon rune, deals an additional 1d6 mental damage, and functions as a +1 striking weapon rune.</p>"},{"n":"Weapon Master","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The graveknight has access to the critical specialization effects of any weapons it wields.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/deadly-spinning-blade-pillar":{"description":"<p>A spinning metal pole covered in deadly blades is hidden in the ceiling, connected to several trigger plates around the room and a hidden control panel built into the bed frame.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 39 Thievery (master) three times on a pillar, or DC 37 Thievery (master) twice on the control panel deactivates the whole trap. Breaking the control panel prevents anyone from disabling the trap using the control panel and prevents the trap from deactivating automatically (see Reset below)</p>","reset":"<p>The trap deactivates and resets after 1 minute.</p>","routine":"<p>(3 actions) The trap uses its first action to make a spinning blade Strike against each adjacent creature. Its second action is to move in a random direction (roll 1d4 to determine the direction), and its third action to make a spinning blade Strike against each adjacent creature.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master) or DC 48 (master) to find the control panel</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Descending Pillar","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature steps on one of the marked trigger plates</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The pillar descends from the ceiling at the marked grid intersection and makes a spinning blade Strike against one adjacent creature (if any). The trap then rolls initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Speed","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>10 feet</p>"},{"n":"Panel Statistics","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Panel Hardness</strong> 15;</p>\n<p><strong>Panel HP</strong> 40 (BT 20)</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/deific-vessel-of-asmodeus":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","truespeech"],"lore":[["Hell Lore",37]],"gear":["Mace","Explorer's Clothing"],"abilities":[{"n":"Choking Ashes","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","fire"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. When a creature ends its turn in the aura, it takes 6d6 fire damage (DC 38 basic Reflex save). A creature that fails this save is also Sickened 2 (Sickened 3 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Mark of Fate","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["curse","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature that slays the deific vessel must succeed at a DC 41 Will save or be visibly marked as anathema to Asmodeus. It gains weakness 15 to unholy and takes a –2 circumstance penalty to Charisma-based skill checks against followers of Asmodeus. Creatures attempting to Track or Gather information about the creature gain a +2 circumstance bonus to their checks. The mark can't be hidden but can be removed by participating in an Atone ritual led by a worshipper of Asmodeus who's 15th level or higher.</p>\n<p>Effect: Mark of Fate (Asmodeus)</p>"},{"n":"Furious Flames","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The vessel's unarmed attacks and any weapon they wield gain the <em>greater flaming</em> and <em>greater grievous</em> runes, and their Strikes gain the critical specialization effects of the appropriate weapon group.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/diabolic-vigor":{"description":"<p>Tendrils of infernal energy reach out from the Inferno Gate like tentacles, infusing the creatures that serve it, even tangentially, with vitality and protection from harm.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 30 Religion (expert) to pray for divine intervention in counterbalancing this infernal influence; DC 35 Arcana (expert), DC 35 Nature (expert), or DC 35 Occultism (expert) to exert a magical force of will greater than the gate's influence; DC 38 Athletics (expert) or Thievery (expert) to disrupt the pentagram surrounding the Inferno Gate; or Dispel Magic (7th rank; counteract DC 30) to cut off the magical energies. Magical checks to disable this hazard can be attempted from up to 30 feet away from the Inferno Gate, but physical checks require physically touching the pentagram; three successes are required to disrupt the diabolic vigor hazard.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action) On its turn, the diabolic vigor hazard empowers the merztorlegon and their bound armies within 200 feet of the Inferno Gate. It grants the siege devil regeneration 20 and reduces their weakness to holy from 20 to 10. The armies gain regeneration 10 and reduce their weakness to area damage and splash damage by 5. These effects last for 1 round.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Burst of Power","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Encounter <strong>E4</strong> begins</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The Inferno Gate sends out beams of reddish energy to all devils and their bound armies within 200 feet, reducing all of their weaknesses by 10 for 1 round. The diabolic vigor hazard then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/disciple-of-the-thread":{"lang":["Azlanti","Common"],"lore":[["Tailoring Lore",33]],"gear":["Explorer's Clothing","Tailoring Toolkit (Sterling)","Key"],"abilities":[{"n":"Sartorial Snag","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An adjacent creature uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The disciple drives several threaded needles through the triggering creature's clothing and pulls, momentarily binding its outfit and restricting movement. The disciple attempts a Tailoring Lore check against the triggering creature's AC. If the triggering creature isn't wearing at least a cloak, sash, tabard, or similar amount of visible cloth, apply a –2 circumstance penalty to this check.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> As success, plus the disciple disrupts the action.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> Threads partly entangle the triggering creature, it becomes Clumsy 1 and takes a –10-foot circumstance penalty to it Speeds until the beginning of its next turn. Any creature within reach of the targeted creature can end these effects with an Interact action.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The triggering creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The disciple becomes Off-Guard until the beginning of their next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Pins and Needles","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The disciple gains access to the critical specialization effects of their sleeve and needle Strikes, with a DC of 34.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The disciple's Strikes deal an additional 2d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Tailor-Made Armaments","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>While wearing clothing worth at least 10 gp, a disciple of thread can cause their sleeves or other parts of their outfit to extend and animate as unarmed Strikes in the flail weapon group. While wielding these sleeves, the cultist can use their Tailoring Lore modifier in place of Athletics to Grapple, Reposition, and Trip. As a free action while carrying a tailoring toolkit, the disciple can Draw mundane sewing needles to use as lethal throwing weapons in the bow weapon group.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/divine-warden-army":{"lang":["Common","Empyrean"],"notes":{"speed":"troop movement"},"abilities":[{"n":"Divine Devastation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine","holy","spirit"],"f":"","d":"<p>Each time the divine warden army loses a segment and when they're reduced to 0 Hit Points, divine energy erupts from the fallen, dealing 8d6 spirit damage to each enemy within a 30-foot emanation (DC 38 basic Will save). On a failure, a creature is also Enfeebled 1 and Stupefied 1 for 1 day (Enfeebled 2 and Stupefied 2 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Divine Lance Fusillade","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["holy","magical"],"f":"","d":"<p>The divine warden army unleashes beams of divine energy. This fusillade is a 10-foot burst within 60 feet that deals 9d6 spirit damage with a DC 37 basic Reflex save. When the divine warden army is reduced to 2 segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Holy Blades","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["holy","magical"],"f":"","d":"<p>The divine wardens make coordinated melee attacks with their swords. Each enemy within a 5-foot emanation must attempt a DC 37 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 2d8+1 slashing damage</p>\n<p>2 4d8+12 slashing damage</p>\n<p>3 6d8+13 slashing damage</p>"},{"n":"Orchestra of Faith","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The divine warden army is a beacon for the faithful. A cleric of Iomedae can channel a Heal spell through a divine warden they can see within 60 feet. The cleric determines any targets or area for the spell as if they were standing in a space of the divine warden army of their choosing.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/dottari-excruciator-division":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"lore":[["Legal Lore",14]],"notes":{"speed":"troop movement"},"flavor":"<p>The dottari serve as Cheliax's elite city guards, assembled and deployed to quash serious threats. Queen Abrogail Thrune I founded the original excruciator divisions to restore order to a nation torn by civil war and not yet fully submissive to Thrune rule. To this day, the dottari are empowered to destroy property (or break a few bones) in carrying out their duties.</p>\n<p>Dottari are trained to neutralize foes nonlethally, but they empowered to use lethal force at their discretion (and often do). They're also famed for their alchemical crossbow bolts—many tipped with fast-acting, explosive glue—ending altercations before they've really begun.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Long Arm of the Law","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature adjacent to the dottari excruciator division leaves a square during a move action it's using</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The excruciators deal 2d8+9 bludgeoning damage to the triggering creature with a DC 25 basic Reflex save. On a critical failure, the creature's move action is disrupted.</p>"},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Bash It Down","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The excruciators make a coordinated effort to shove outward with their shields, taking down opponents and impediments alike. The troop attempts to either Shove or Trip each enemy in a 5-foot emanation and Force open each object in a 5-foot emanation. The troop rolls a single Athletics check and compares the result to each target's appropriate DC. The troop doesn't take a penalty for not having a crowbar. It's possible for the troop to get a different degree of success for each target. The troop can't automatically Stride after any creature they successfully Shove.</p>"},{"n":"Beat the Lawbreakers","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["magical"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The excruciators swing their maces in a coordinated melee attack against each enemy in a 5-foot emanation (DC 25 basic Reflex save). The damage depends on the number of actions. The excruciators can choose to deal nonlethal damage with this attack.</p>\n<p>1 1d6+2 bludgeoning</p>\n<p>2 2d6+11 bludgeoning</p>\n<p>3 3d6+14 bludgeoning</p>"},{"n":"Stop Where You Are","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["magical"],"f":"","d":"<p>The excruciators draw or reload their crossbows with special hindering bolts, then launch a ranged attack in the form of a volley. This volley is a 10-foot burst within 80 feet that deals 4d6 piercing damage (DC 25 basic Reflex save). When the dottari excruciator division is reduced to 2 or fewer segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst. On a failure, a creature also takes a –10-foot circumstance penalty to its Speeds for 1 round. On a critical failure, a creature also gains the Immobilized condition (Escape).</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/dream-drowner":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Sakvroth","Thalassic","telepathy 100 feet"],"lore":[["Architecture Lore",25],["Cave Lore",25]],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"flavor":"<p>Dream drowners are anemone-like predators from Orv's flooded vaults. A dream drowner indefinitely parasitizes and mentally controls a host to serve as its mount as it seeks out the thoughts of thinking prey to consume. So far, any attempt to communicate with these creatures elicits aggression, yet the beings' behavior demonstrates extraordinary intelligence.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Entrancing Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","occult","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet.</p>\n<p>The dream drowner's tentacles move with hypnotic grace. When a creature ends its turn in the dream drowner's aura, it must attempt a DC 32 Will save, becoming Stupefied 1 on a failure (or increasing its stupefied value by 1, to a maximum of 4). The dream drowner can deactivate or activate this aura by using a single action, which has the concentrate trait.</p>"},{"n":"Eldritch Toxin","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["curse","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature touched by a dream drowner's tentacles must succeed at a DC 29 Will save or become Stunned 1 (Stunned 2 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Entangled Thoughts","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature affected by a dream drowner's Dominate spell becomes Confused for 1 minute after the <em>dominate</em> spell ends. The creature can attempt a DC 32 Will save at the end of each of its turns to end the condition.</p>"},{"n":"Mind Leech","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a creature fails or critically fails a Will save against a dream drowner's occult innate spells, the creature takes 1d6 nonlethal mental damage per rank of the spell.</p>"},{"n":"Subjugate Minds","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>A dream drowner assaults the minds of distracted creatures. Each creature within a 20-foot emanation that has the Fascinated or stupefied condition takes 10d8 mental damage (DC 32 basic Will save).</p>\n<p>The dream drowner can't use this ability again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Tentacle Flurry","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The dream drowner makes a tentacle Strike against each creature within its reach. These Strikes count toward the dream drowner's multiple attack penalty, but the multiple attack penalty doesn't increase until after the dream drowner makes all its attacks.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/elder-sweet-hag":{"lang":["Aklo","Chthonian","Common","Fey","Jotun","Daemonic","Diabolic","Truespeech"],"lore":[["Cooking Lore",24]],"notes":{"saves":"+1 to all saves vs. magic"},"flavor":"<p>Sweet hags use bright colors, pleasant visages, and sugary treats to draw in children and the young at heart. Their favorite prey is impoverished youngsters who are unlikely to be missed—sweet hags offer them food and a veneer of kindness before devouring the hapless child. Sweet hags also enchant their food to magically charm others, often using these bespelled servitors to handle all of their busywork. Though they present a lovely and generous face to the world, they turn vicious when insulted or defied. A sweet hag's true form is a dribbling mass of flesh with gumdrop eyes, often resembling melting taffy.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Hags are malevolent predators who use magic and manipulation to lure children and young adults into their clutches. Though their true forms are eldritch and horrifying, hags spend much of their lives disguised as ordinary women. They seek out targets who are unhappy, innocent, or otherwise vulnerable, preying on their weaknesses before snatching them up. The typical hag is abusive, controlling, and narcissistic. Though less malicious hags possibly exist, they rarely reveal their true forms, making them nearly impossible to find.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Coven","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>A sweet hag adds Charm, Honeyed Words, and Outcast's Curse to their coven's spells.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><p>This monster can form a coven with two or more other creatures who also have the coven ability. This involves performing an 8-hour ceremony with all prospective coven members. After the coven is formed, each of its members gains elite adjustments, adjusting their levels accordingly. Coven members can sense other members' locations and conditions by spending a single action, which has the concentrate trait, and can sense what another coven member is sensing as a two-action activity, which has the concentrate trait as well.</p>\n<p>Covens also grant spells and rituals to their members, but these can be cast only in cooperation between three coven members who are all within 30 feet of one another. A coven member can contribute to a coven spell with a single action that has the concentrate trait. If two coven members have contributed these actions within the last round, a third member can cast a coven spell on her turn by spending the normal spellcasting actions. A coven can cast its coven spells an unlimited number of times but can cast only one coven spell each round. All covens grant the 8th-rank Cursed Metamorphosis spell and all the following spells, which the coven can cast at any rank up to 5th: Augury, Charm, Clairaudience, Clairvoyance, Dream Message, Illusory Disguise, Illusory Scene, Scouting Eye, and Talking Corpse. Individual creatures with the coven ability also grant additional spells to any coven they join. A coven can also cast the Control Weather ritual, with a DC of 23 instead of the standard DC.</p>\n<p>If a coven member's departure or death brings the coven below three members, the remaining members keep their elite adjustments for 24 hours, but without enough members to contribute the necessary actions, they can't cast coven spells.</p></p>"},{"n":"At-Will Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster can cast its at-will spells any number of times without using up spell slots.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Betraying Touch","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The sweet hag touches a creature that doesn't realize the hag is an enemy. The betrayed creature is affected by soporific strike with a –4 circumstance penalty to their saving throw.</p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","occult","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p>The sweet hag can take on the appearance of any Medium humanoid woman. This doesn't change their Speed or their attack and damage bonuses with their Strikes, but it might change the damage type their Strikes deal (typically to bludgeoning).</p>\n<hr>\n<p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"Poisoned Candy","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The sweet hag casts an innate spell that can normally target 1 creature on a piece of food, typically a sweet treat. The spell is stored in the food. The first creature that eats any of the food is affected by the spell and takes a –4 circumstance penalty to their saving throw against that effect.</p>"},{"n":"Soporific Touch","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["incapacitation","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature damaged by a sweet hag's claw must succeed at a DC 32 Fortitude save or be Enfeebled 1 for 1 day.</p>\n<p>If the creature critically fails or fails this save while already enfeebled by soporific strike, it falls Unconscious and dreams of eating delicious sweets; this is a mental sleep effect. If not woken up before 1 minute passes, the creature wakes up automatically.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/elven-waverider-troop":{"lang":["Common","Elven","Fey"],"lore":[["Ocean Lore",21]],"notes":{"speed":"troop movement"},"abilities":[{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Thrusting Flurry","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The waveriders launch coordinated attacks against each enemy in a 5-foot emanation with a DC 27 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 1d8+6 piercing damage</p>\n<p>2 3d8+6 piercing damage</p>\n<p>3 4d8+9 piercing damage</p>"},{"n":"Wavecrash","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["water"],"f":"","d":"<p>The waveriders conjure a cresting wave beneath their feet and use it ride down their enemies. The waveriders Stride up to double their Speed and can move through the spaces of Medium or smaller creatures or troops composed of Medium or smaller creatures. Creatures in the path of the waveriders take 1d8+6 bludgeoning damage (DC 30 basic Reflex save).</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/feedback-flow":{"description":"<p>The fetid material in this pit sloshes around in a disgusting feedback loop, filled with large pieces of solid trash that risk bludgeoning creatures inside it to death!</p>","disable":"<p>DC 27 Acrobatics or DC 27 Thievery (trained) to move without causing a wave of filth, or DC 30 Athletics or DC 30 Crafting (trained) to stabilize the trash heap and prevent it from flowing; three successes are required to fully stabilize and disable the hazard.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 to 3 actions) The feedback flow hazard uses up to 3 actions to make flowing trash Strikes against living creatures that take move actions inside the refuse pit (area <strong>E7</strong>) but can only target an individual creature once per round. The ofalths, used to living in this pit, don't trigger these attacks. Additionally, any non-ofalth creature that ends its turn inside the refuse pit must attempt a DC 36 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Sickened 1 until the end of its next turn, then is immune to this effect for 1 minute.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is sickened 1.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Sickened 2.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Wobbling Waves","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Any Medium or larger non-ofalth creature takes a move action inside area <strong>E7</strong></p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The feedback flow makes a flowing trash Strike against the triggering creature and then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/fiendish-mantis":{"flavor":"<p>These gigantic mantids make their homes within prehistoric forests.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>These predators possess lightning-quick forelegs and a bone-breaking bite.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Ship-Bound","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The mantis is fused to the ship and moves where the ship moves. It doesn't occupy a space of its own but is treated as being in the front 20-foot-by-20-foot space of the ship for the purpose of making attacks and being targeted.</p>"},{"n":"Blood-Scent","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>After consuming the blood of a living creature, the mantis can track it (as the locate spell, but it functions over running water and has a range of 300 miles).</p>"},{"n":"Fling","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The deadly mantis flings a Grabbed creature into the air, up to 30 feet overhead and up to 30 feet away from the mantis (the creature takes damage from the fall as normal). If the flung creature lands on another creature, the creature it lands on takes the same amount of bludgeoning damage with a DC 31 basic Reflex save.</p>"},{"n":"Rending Mandibles","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The mantis makes a mandibles Strike against a creature it has Grabbed. If that Strike hits and the creature is wearing armor with Hardness 12 or lower, the armor is broken. This Strike doesn't further damage armor that's already broken.</p>"},{"n":"Sudden Strike","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>On the first round of combat, creatures that haven't acted are Off-Guard to the deadly mantis.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/first-class-cavalry":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Warfare Lore",24]],"notes":{"speed":"troop movement"},"flavor":"<p>Soldiers who participate in multiple campaigns of war gain the experience necessary to become their military's finest fighting forces. first-class cavalry troops are deployed on battlefields where winning the day is of the utmost importance.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"No Retreat","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>These soldiers have been extensively trained to hold their ground no matter the situation. If any effect would force the first-class cavalry to move, reduce the distance by 10 feet. Any time they would be affected by the Fleeing condition, the first-class cavalry is instead Slowed 2 for the same duration.</p>"},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>HP</strong> 240 (4 segments); <strong>Thresholds</strong> 160 (3 segments), 80 (2 segments)</p>\n<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Bolt Salvo","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The first-class cavalry draws, loads, and shoots a salvo from their crossbows. The salvo is a 10-foot burst within 120 feet that deals 4d8 piercing damage (DC 30 basic Reflex save). When the first-class cavalry is reduced to 2 segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Clash of Steel","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p>1 to 3</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The first-class cavalry attacks each enemy in a 5-foot emanation, with a DC 29 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 2d6+1 slashing damage</p>\n<p>2 4d6+10 slashing damage</p>\n<p>3 4d6+18 slashing damage</p>"},{"n":"Drilled in Formations","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The first-class cavalry uses Change Formation. An first-class cavalry unit typically knows the marching column and wedge formations.</p>"},{"n":"First-class Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The first-class cavalry rushes forward with a hunger for battle. They Stride up to twice their Speed. At the end of their movement, each enemy within a 5-foot emanation takes 2d6+5 slashing damage, with a DC 30 basic Reflex save.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/first-class-vordines":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Warfare Lore",24]],"notes":{"speed":"troop movement"},"flavor":"<p>Soldiers who participate in multiple campaigns of war gain the experience necessary to become their military's finest fighting forces. First-class vordines troops are deployed on battlefields where winning the day is of the utmost importance.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"No Retreat","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>These soldiers have been extensively trained to hold their ground no matter the situation. If any effect would force the first-class vordines to move, reduce the distance by 10 feet. Any time they would be affected by the Fleeing condition, the first-class vordines is instead Slowed 2 for the same duration.</p>"},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>HP</strong> 240 (4 segments); <strong>Thresholds</strong> 160 (3 segments), 80 (2 segments)</p>\n<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Bolt Salvo","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The first-class vordines draw, load, and shoot a salvo from their crossbows. The salvo is a 10-foot burst within 120 feet that deals 4d8 piercing damage (DC 30 basic Reflex save). When the first-class vordines are reduced to 2 segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Clash of Steel","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p>1 to 3</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The first-class vordines attack each enemy in a 5-foot emanation, with a DC 29 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 2d6+1 slashing damage</p>\n<p>2 4d6+10 slashing damage</p>\n<p>3 4d6+18 slashing damage</p>"},{"n":"Drilled in Formations","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The first-class vordines uses Change Formation. An first-class vordines unit typically knows the marching column and wedge formations.</p>"},{"n":"First-class Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The first-class vordines rushes forward with a hunger for battle. They Stride up to twice their Speed. At the end of their movement, each enemy within a 5-foot emanation takes 2d6+5 slashing damage, with a DC 30 basic Reflex save.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/floor-be-gone":{"description":"<p>Hinged boards prop the massive paving stones into place on the causeway.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 27 Crafting (expert) to reinforce the stones of this causeway or DC 29 Thievery (master) to jam the hinges on the boards</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Oops, There It Goes!","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature moves through a marked square and fails a secret DC 5 Flat</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The board's hinges release, causing the paving stones to drop—along with any creatures in the marked area—to the ground below. Affected creatures can attempt to Grab an edge (DC 29). Creatures that fall take 4d12+26 bludgeoning damage (DC 29 basic Reflex save) as well as the typical falling damage.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/fog-hound":{"lang":["Diabolic","(Can't Speak Any Language)"],"flavor":"<p>Believed to be bred by the Kings of Hell themselves within vast kennels, greater hell hounds are the favored guards and hunting hounds of powerful fiends and, rarely, mortals who worship them and have earned their favor.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Hell hounds are fiendish, extraplanar canines hailing from the Pit that can hunt down quarry and breathe supernatural gouts of flame. They are temperamental and quick to exhibit aggressive behavior.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Hellish Revenge","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The greater hell hound is critically hit by any Strike</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The greater hell hound's Hellfire Breath recharges. They can immediately use it as part of this reaction.</p>"},{"n":"Fog Born","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The fog hound's breathe fog and are composed of mist. Their jaws Strike and Hellfire Breath deal cold damage instead of fire damage and have the cold trait.</p>"},{"n":"Hellfire Breath","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["cold","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The hell hound breathes flames that deal 10d6 cold damage to all creatures in a 15-foot cone (DC 28 basic Reflex save.)</p>\n<p>The hell hound can't use Hellfire Breath again for 1d4 rounds. If the greater hell hound would take cold damage or be targeted by a cold effect, their Hellfire Breath recharges.</p>"},{"n":"Pack Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The greater hell hound's Strikes deal 1d8 extra damage to creatures within the reach of at least two of their allies.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/force-and-flame":{"description":"<p>Four invisible runes on a large crate conjure jets of flame and whips of force when someone tries to open the container.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 45 Thievery (master) to erase each rune, DC 48 Arcana (master) to channel energy from one rune into another, destroying both, or Dispel Magic (8th rank; counteract DC 45) to counteract each rune; a PC can choose to disable a fire rune or a force rune (or choose randomly)</p>","reset":"<p>The runes deactivate after 1 minute, but if at least one rune remains, the trap reactivates 1 round after that.</p>","routine":"<p>(4 actions) The trap has 1 fewer action for each rune that's been disabled or destroyed; whether that rune was a fire rune or a force rune affects the actions the trap can take. On the trap's initiative, the two fire runes each blast 30-foot cones of flame as an action in opposite directions that deal 12d6 fire damage (DC 44 basic Reflex save). Then the two force runes each make a force whip Strike as an action against different targets.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Blinding Alarm","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["visual"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature tries to open the crate without removing the runes</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The four runes become active with a flash of red light. Each creature in a 30-foot emanation must attempt a DC 42 Reflex save. The trap then rolls initiative.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is slightly dazed by the flash, taking a –2 circumstance penalty to their initiative.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is Blinded for 1 round and takes a –2 circumstance penalty to their initiative.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target is blinded for 1 minute and takes a –4 circumstance penalty to their initiative.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/glittercrag-strix":{"lang":["Common","Strix"],"gear":["Spear","Corundum Shield"],"abilities":[{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Heavy Wingbeats","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Glittercrag strix uses their powerful muscles to gain altitude through raw power. They can Step twice and Strike once in any order. Instead of Stepping, the strix can instead Fly up to 10 feet, ignoring difficult terrain caused by flying upward.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/golden-fiend-sister":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"lore":[["Martial Arts Lore",30]],"gear":["Handwraps of Mighty Blows","Khakkhara","Dart","Bands of Force","Keys"],"focus":3,"abilities":[{"n":"Disrupt Qi","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["void"],"f":"","d":"<p>The Golden Fiend Sister attempts an unarmed Strike against a living creature. On a hit, the creature takes 3d6 persistent void damage and is Enfeebled 2 until the persistent damage ends.</p>"},{"n":"Flurry of Blows","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The Golden Fiend Sister makes two fist Strikes. If both hit the same creature, combine their damage for the purpose of resistances and weaknesses. The sister can substitute any number of the attacks with khakkara Strikes or attempts to Grapple, Reposition, Shove, or Trip.</p>"},{"n":"Monastic Weaponry","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A Golden Fiend Sister can substitute a khakkara Strike for any ability that requires a fist Strike.</p>"},{"n":"One-Millimeter Punch","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>2 or 3</p><hr><p>The Golden Fiend Sister makes a single, carefully controlled fist Strike that deals 2 additional dice of damage, or 4 additional dice if she spent 3 actions. If this damages the target, the Golden Fiend Sister can choose to make the target attempt a DC 38 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is pushed back 5 feet.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is pushed back 10 feet.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target is pushed back 10 feet for each action the Golden Fiend Sister spent on OneMillimeter Punch.</p>"},{"n":"Powerful Fists","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Golden Fiend Sister's fist Strikes don't take penalties when making lethal attacks, and her fist Strikes are treated as adamantine, cold iron, and silver.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/gorthoklek":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Empyrean","telepathy 100 feet"],"gear":["Spiked Chain"],"notes":{"hp":"regeneration 30 (deactivated by holy)","saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>When an army of devils invades to bathe a region in bloodshed and hellfire, it is likely that one of the nessaris masterminded the incursion. Cunning, powerful, and ruthless, nessaris often serve the archdevils directly. They rule infernal duchies, subjugate mortal worlds, and usurp infernal rivals using unparalleled despotism and calculated ferocity. To realize their tyrannical machinations, nessaris claim mortal souls that they corrupt into ort servants, which can then be shaped and transformed through infernal manipulation into the terrifying devils that form Hell's formidable legions. They often select the most wicked and vicious orts for their armies, drawing upon these lesser devils' depravity during powerful magical ceremonies to create hideous and terrifying abominations that can cow and eviscerate the nessari's enemies.</p>\n<p>Each nessari is crafted deep within the nightmarish bowels of Nessus, the ninth layer of Hell, to serve the whims of archdevils and infernal dukes. Those nessaris that don't leave Nessus to command infernal legions in the upper layers of Hell often form the courts of Hell's elite, gathering cronies and sects that shape Hell's political landscape through subterfuge and manipulation. But many nessaris see themselves as living embodiments of hellfire, the all-encompassing wrath of Hell, and thus prefer to dwell in realms consumed by fire. In Avernus, Dis, Malebolge, Nessus, and Phlegethon, nessaris build vast citadels of brimstone wreathed in flame to lord over.</p>\n<p>Rather than being above the constant power struggles of the diabolic ranks, nessaris are in the thick of it. Even apocalyptic schemes to conquer or despoil mortal worlds usually begin from a desire to claw a single rank up the immortal hierarchy of Hell. For this reason, the best, yet also most dangerous, ally against a nessari is the nessari next to them.</p>\n<p>Nessaris tower over other devils, standing at least 16 feet tall, weighing over 1,000 pounds, and brandishing wingspans in excess of 20 feet.</p>\n<h2>Infernal Dukes</h2>\n<p>Elite members of Hell's political infrastructure and leadership hierarchy, the dukes of Hell are chosen from among the most tyrannical, oppressive, and conniving devils. While not all infernal dukes are nessaris, a nessari's natural disposition toward conquest and oppression often makes them an ideal candidate for this position. To create an infernal duke, adjust the nessari to be between 21st and 25th level. Because of their physical prowess, manipulative nature, and powerful spellcasting abilities, infernal dukes make excellent villains for long-running campaigns.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Masters of corruption and architects of conquest, devils seek both to tempt mortal life to join in their pursuit of all things profane and to spread tyranny throughout all worlds. The temptations they offer mortals range from great powers granted by the signing of an infernal contract to twisted favors following a whispered pledge to a diabolic patron, or any number of even subtler exchanges. Those who succumb to these temptations find themselves consigned to an afterlife of endless torment in the pits of Hell, wherein the only hope of escape lies in the chance of being promoted to become a devil in the infernal ranks.</p>\n<p>Every devil has a specific role to play in the upkeep of the remorseless bureaucratic machine that is Hell, from soldiers and scholars to inquisitors, lawyers, judges, and executioners. Lowly orts perform subservient labor to more powerful and specialized devils, such as infantry and contract devils, while the greatest nessaris command entire infernal armies.</p>\n<p>Asmodeus stands at the apex of the structure he created, but the layers below him are marked by a constant jockeying for position. Most diabolic plans ultimately serve to improve the schemer's place in the hierarchy.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Greater Darkvision","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with greater darkvision can see perfectly well in areas of darkness and dim light, though such vision is in black and white only. A creature with greater darkvision can see through even forms of magical darkness.</p></p>"},{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"At-Will Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster can cast its at-will spells any number of times without using up spell slots.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Regeneration 30 (Deactivated by Holy)","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>This monster regains the listed number of Hit Points each round at the beginning of its turn. Its Dying condition never increases beyond Dying 3 as long as its regeneration is active. However, if it takes damage of a type listed in the regeneration entry, its regeneration deactivates until the end of its next turn. Deactivate the regeneration before applying any damage of a listed type, since that damage might kill the monster by bringing it to Dying 4.</p></p>"},{"n":"Frightful Presence","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet. DC 44 Will</p><hr><p><p>A creature that first enters the area must attempt a Will save.</p>\n<p>Regardless of the result of the saving throw, the creature is temporarily immune to this monster's Frightful Presence for 1 minute.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected by the presence.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 4.</p></p>"},{"n":"General's Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>150 feet.</p>\n<p>Commanded or allied unholy creatures in the aura of lower level than Gorthoklek gain a +1 circumstance bonus to attack rolls, damage rolls, AC, saves, and skill checks.</p>\n<p>Once per turn, a commanded or allied unholy creature in this aura can Step as a free action.</p>\n<p>Effect: General's Aura</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Chain Sweep","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Gorthoklek makes a spiked chain Strike and compares the attack roll result to the AC of up to three foes, each of whom must be within his melee reach and no more than 10 feet from each other. Gorthoklek rolls damage only once and applies it to each creature hit. A creature that's critically hit is also knocked Prone. Chain Sweep counts as two attacks for his multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p>Gorthoklek takes on the shape of any Large or smaller humanoid. This doesn't change his Speed or attack and damage bonuses with his Strikes but might change the damage type his Strikes deal (typically to bludgeoning).</p><hr><p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>2d10+19 bludgeoning, DC 45 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC.</p></p>"},{"n":"Fast Swoop","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Gorthoklek Flies and makes a wing Strike at any point during its movement.</p>"},{"n":"Masterful Quickened Casting","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> If the nessari's next action is to cast an 8th-rank or lower innate spell, reduce the number of actions to cast it by 1 (minimum 1 action).</p>"},{"n":"Nessari Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 45 Fortitude</p>\n<p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 10 rounds</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 6d6 poison damage and Drained 1 (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 8d6 poison damage and Drained 2 (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 9d6 poison damage and Drained 3 (1 round)</p>"},{"n":"Shape Devils","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine","downtime"],"f":"","d":"<p>Gorthoklek reshapes a large number of orts within a 600-foot emanation into more powerful devils to swell Hell's legions. Gorthoklek must have available the number of orts listed on the table below.</p><table><thead><tr><th><p>Devil Level</p></th><th><p>Number of Orts</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>4 or below</p></td><td><p>4</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5-6</p></td><td><p>8</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7-8</p></td><td><p>16</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>9-10</p></td><td><p>32</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>11-12</p></td><td><p>64</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>13-14</p></td><td><p>128</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>15-16</p></td><td><p>256</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>17-18</p></td><td><p>512</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>19-20</p></td><td><p>1.024</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Gorthoklek can shape 100 orts per day, to a maximum of 1,100 orts in 11 days. Devils created in this way whose level is 19 or lower are in thrall to Gorthoklek and follow his orders. At the end of the Shape Devils activity, Gorthoklek attempts an incredibly hard Religion check of the desired devil's level, with results as follows. If Gorthoklek gets a critical failure, he gets a failure instead.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> Gorthoklek shapes two devils from the massed orts instead of one.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> Gorthoklek shapes a devil of the desired type and level.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The devil shaped from the orts is 2 levels lower than the intended devil.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Gorthoklek fails to shape any devils and draws the ire of an archdevil for his waste of resources.</p>"},{"n":"Unholy Bloodshed","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Gorthoklek critically succeeds at an attack roll against a holy creature with his Unholy Spiked Chain</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The target takes 3d8 bleed.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/grachius-alazario":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"lore":[["Legal Lore",33]],"gear":["+2 Greater Striking Staff of Fire (Major)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Unyielding Purpose","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Grachius would be reduced to 0 HP</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Grachius has a divine immolation spell remaining</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Grachius refuses to disappoint Abrogail Thrune; he stabilizes at 1 HP just long enough to cast divine immolation, centered on himself. He dies, immolated in the hellish flames.</p>"},{"n":"Monologue","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Grachius ceaselessly expounds upon the ongoing Hellish apocalypse and the futility of his enemies' efforts to stop it. He gains a +1 status bonus to Will saves and a +2 status bonus to damage rolls with his spells. Each time he takes this action again, the bonuses increase by 1 and 2, respectively. The monologue ends (and the bonuses are lost) if Grachius becomes unable to act or speak, or if he ends his turn without having taken this action.</p>"},{"n":"Overwhelming Energy","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["spellshape"],"f":"","d":"<p>If the next action Grachius uses is to Cast a Spell, the spell ignores 20 resistance to energy damage. This applies to all damage the spell deals, including persistent damage and damage caused by an ongoing effect of the spell. A creature's immunities are unaffected.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/greater-hellcat":{"lang":["Diabolic","Can't speak any language, Fiendish telepathy 100 feet"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"flavor":"<p>Hellcats are devious predators native to the fiery pits of Hell. While the fiendish creatures resemble undead skeletal smilodons, bones smoking with heat and dripping with boiling blood, they're actually living hellspawn whose transparent flesh reveals their burning skeleton. A typical hellcat is 9 feet long and weighs 1,000 pounds.</p>\n<p>Left to their own devices, hellcats spend their time hunting. As fiendish creatures, they don't need mortal sustenance but devour prey for the sheer pleasure of inflicting pain. They're also far more intelligent than most assume, and they resent being treated as unintelligent animals; those who treat a hellcat thusly might find themselves made into a trophy for its pack, as a hellcat will go to great lengths to coordinate elaborate revenge upon any who fail to show them proper respect.</p>\n<p>Though they can't speak, hellcats know Diabolic and can communicate by telepathy with any creature capable of speech. They rarely say much except to whisper threats and acknowledge the orders of their diabolic masters.</p>\n<p>Hellcats are quick to retreat if clearly outmatched or up against foes they're unable to reach, but they never forget prey that escapes them.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Fiendish Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>This functions as telepathy, except that the greater hellcat can speak mentally to any creature, regardless of language. This doesn't grant the greater hellcat the ability to understand what the other creature is thinking, unless that creature also understands Diabolic.</p><hr><p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Elusive Terror","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>A greater hellcat can live within the fears of others and use their dread to hide from sight. The greater hellcat can Hide in the presence of Frightened creatures. If successful, the greater hellcat becomes Hidden from frightened creatures as if it moved behind cover or into concealment, but must otherwise Hide normally from non-frightened creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Vengeful Growl","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The greater hellcat is critically hit by any Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The greater hellcat's Menacing Growl recharges. The creature that dealt the triggering Strike must succeed at a DC 37 Will save or become Frightened 2 (Frightened 4 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Fearful Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hellcat deals an additional 3d6 precision damage to Frightened creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Hell Pack Mindlink","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The greater hellcat telepathically links its senses to all other hellcats within 100 feet for 10 minutes. It loses this contact with any hellcat that moves out of a 100-foot radius. While linked to at least one ally, the greater hellcat can't be flanked and gains a +2 status bonus to Will saving throws.</p>"},{"n":"Menacing Growl","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The greater hellcat produces a low growl to disorient and frighten foes. The hellcat can cause this vocalization to originate from somewhere else within 30 feet. Non-fiends in a 15-foot burst must attempt a DC 37 Will save. The hellcat can't issue another Menacing Growl for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and is temporarily immune for 24 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 4.</p>"},{"n":"Pounce","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The greater hellcat Strides and makes a Strike at the end of that movement. If the greater hellcat began this action Hidden, it remains hidden until after the ability's Strike.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/guardian-guises":{"description":"<p>Apparitions of Aroden in his various 12 guises (the shepherd, soldier, tailor, thief, and more) emerge in pairs to defend this room.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 43 Diplomacy (master), DC 43 Intimidation (master), or DC 43 Religion (expert); three successes are required to convince the trap that Aroden is truly dead, causing the Spiritual Guardians to hesitate and protest before fading away</p>","reset":"<p>1 day or after Kaisentia spends 10 minutes here in focused prayer</p>","routine":"<p>(2 actions; spirit) The hazard Sustains both spiritual guardians, either attacking or protecting at Kaisentia's direction. Once per round, if fewer than two <em>spiritual guardians</em> are present, the hazard conjures one new <em>spiritual guardian</em> from one of the statues as an action. Each statue can create only one <em>spiritual guardian</em> in this way before needing to be reset.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Last Azlanti's Defense","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["divine","spirit"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Kaisentia rolls initiative</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Two 9th-rank Spiritual Guardian spells resembling ghostly simulacra of Aroden in two of his 12 guises emerge from their corresponding statues. One moves to an unoccupied space within the statue's line of effect and makes an attack against an adjacent creature hostile to Kaisentia (spell attack modifier of +33, 5d8 force damage). The other moves to an unoccupied space adjacent to Kaisentia and protects her (90 Hit Points). The hazard rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/haunted-knife-collection":{"description":"<p>Crates of knives and daggers shine with ill intent.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 26 Religion (master) to exorcise the spirits, DC 33 Crafting (expert) to damage the knives, or Dispel Magic (5th rank; counteract DC 29) to counteract the crate</p>","reset":"<p>The spirits in the hazard reactivate after 10 minutes.</p>","routine":"<p>(3 actions) The knife collection identifies targets. It first moves to have as many living creatures in its space as possible within a single Fly action, then attempts dagger Strikes against living creatures in its space.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master) or Detect Magic</p>","abilities":[{"n":"10,000 Stabs","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["magical"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A living creature touches one of the crates</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> A cloud of knives rises from the boxes in a 10-foot radius around the touched crate and stabs all creatures in its area, dealing 10d4 slashing damage (DC 34 basic Reflex save). The hazard then rolls initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Speed","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Fly 15 feet</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/hellfire-hydra":{"lang":["Diabolic","Pyric"],"notes":{"hp":"hellfire regeneration","ac":"all-around vision","per":"smoke vision"},"abilities":[{"n":"Smoke Vision","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hellfire hydra ignores the Concealed condition from smoke.</p>"},{"n":"All-Around Vision","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>This monster can see in all directions simultaneously and therefore can't be flanked.</p></p>"},{"n":"Hellfire Regeneration","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hellfire hydra has regeneration equal to 5 × the number of heads it has. If a hellfire hydra's body is missing any heads and the remaining stumps haven't been snuffed out, the hydra attempts a DC 42 Fortitude save after it regains Hit Points from regeneration. On a success, one non-snuffed stump regrows two heads; on a critical success, two nonsnuffed stumps regrow into two heads each. The hellfire hydra can never grow more than 10 heads. The hellfire hydra's regeneration only fully deactivates if all its heads are destroyed and all stumps are snuffed out, at which point it dies.</p><hr><p><p>This monster regains the listed number of Hit Points each round at the beginning of its turn. Its Dying condition never increases beyond Dying 3 as long as its regeneration is active. However, if it takes damage of a type listed in the regeneration entry, its regeneration deactivates until the end of its next turn. Deactivate the regeneration before applying any damage of a listed type, since that damage might kill the monster by bringing it to Dying 4.</p></p>"},{"n":"Head Regrowth","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A hellfire hydra has five heads. A creature can attempt to sever one of the hydra's heads by specifically targeting it and dealing damage equal to the head's Hit Points. A head that isn't completely severed returns to full Hit Points at the end of any creature's turn.</p>\n<p>A hellfire hydra can regrow a severed head using hellfire regeneration. A creature can prevent this regrowth by dealing damage to the stump with a cold or water effect, snuffing out its flames. Single-target cold or water effects need to be targeted at a specific stump, but effects that deal splash damage or affect areas covering the hellfire hydra's whole space snuff out all stumps if they deal damage and have the cold or water trait. If the attack that destroys a head deals any damage with the cold or water trait, the stump is snuffed out instantly. If all five heads are snuffed out, the hydra dies.</p><hr><p><strong>Hydra Head</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Hit Points</strong> 50</p></li><li><p><strong>Immunities</strong> Area Damage</p></li><li><p><strong>Weaknesses</strong> Cold 15, Holy 10, Water 10</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Hellfire Hydra Heads</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Heads","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A hellfire hydra gains an extra reaction per round for each of its heads beyond the first, which it can use only to make Reactive Strikes. It can't use more than 1 reaction on the same triggering action, even if a creature leaves several squares within its reach, and the hydra must use a different head for each Reactive Strike it makes. Whenever one of the hellfire hydra's heads is destroyed, the hydra loses 1 of its extra reactions per round.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike (See Reactive Heads)","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Unholy Heat","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","fire","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>10 feet, 9d6 fire damage, DC 38 basic Reflex save</p>"},{"n":"Conflagration of Jaws","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["attack","fire"],"f":"","d":"<p>The hellfire hydra slams each of its heads into the ground, where they explode before quickly reforming. The hellfire hydra creates a number of 5-foot bursts within 10 feet equal to its current number of heads. These bursts can't overlap. Each creature in a burst takes 6d6 fire damage (DC 40 basic Reflex save). This counts as a number of attacks equal to the number of heads the hellfire hydra has toward the hydra's multiple attack penalty.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/hellfire-tornado":{"description":"<p>The very air catches fire from the heat of a dragon's breath, causing a burning tornado.</p>","disable":"<p>The Hellfire tornado can't be disabled—only endured. It ends after 5 rounds.</p>","reset":"<p>Once 5 rounds pass, the Hellfire tornado dissipates and doesn't reset.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action; air, fire) The Hellfire tornado—a 15-footdiameter column 80 feet tall—moves 60 feet down the street. It can move through creatures' spaces, and creatures can move into its space, though the tornado's space is difficult terrain. Each creature the tornado moves through or each creature that ends its turn in the tornado's area takes 4d10 bludgeoning plus 4d6 fire damage (DC 40 basic Reflex save). A creature can be affected by the tornado only once per round.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and rises 10 feet into the air as it's engulfed by the tornado (Escape). While engulfed, a creature is Grabbed and Slowed 1, and if it doesn't have a fly Speed, it gains a 10-foot fly Speed until it either reaches the ground or ceases to be in the tornado's area, potentially falling when the hazard ends or when it leaves the tornado's area. A creature engulfed by the tornado moves along with it on the tornado's turn.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, except the creature takes double damage and rises 20 feet into the air.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master) <br></p>","abilities":[{"n":"Burning Winds","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["air","fire"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Kandarlu breathes flame onto the streets below</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The back draft from the dragon's breath washes over the PCs. Each creature on the street must attempt a DC 44 Fortitude save. The Hellfire tornado then forms at one end of the street, and the hazard rolls initiative.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is knocked Prone from the wind.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is knocked prone from the wind and gains weakness 10 to fire damage caused by the Hellfire tornado.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the weakness is 15. The creature is also Fatigued from the heat.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/hellknight-amalgamite":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Draconic"],"lore":[["Cheliax Lore",27]],"notes":{"hp":"regeneration 10 (deactivated by piercing)"},"abilities":[{"n":"Regeneration 10 (Deactivated by Piercing)","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>This monster regains the listed number of Hit Points each round at the beginning of its turn. Its Dying condition never increases beyond Dying 3 as long as its regeneration is active. However, if it takes damage of a type listed in the regeneration entry, its regeneration deactivates until the end of its next turn. Deactivate the regeneration before applying any damage of a listed type, since that damage might kill the monster by bringing it to Dying 4.</p></p>"},{"n":"Destabilizing Field","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura"],"f":"","d":"<p>40 feet.</p>\n<p>A creature that begins its turn within the area feels its body begin to stretch and must succeed at a DC 33 Fortitude save or become destabilized. A destabilized creature emits a 10-foot destabilizing field aura and becomes Sickened 1. The destabilization ends when the creature is no longer sickened. A creature that succeeds at its saving throw against the aura is temporarily immune to all destabilizing fields for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Displace","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The amalgamite is hit by a Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The amalgamite Repositions itself or Transposes itself with another creature. If the amalgamite successfully Transposes its location, it and any transposed creature take half damage from the triggering Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Reposition","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>The amalgamite teleports into an unoccupied space it can see within 50 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Transpose","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>The amalgamite chooses up to two destabilized creatures it can see within 50 feet and swaps their positions, or moves one such creature to an unoccupied space it can see within range. If the amalgamite chooses two creatures, it can choose itself as a target, but both targets must be the same size. An unwilling creature can attempt a DC 33 Will save. If either target succeeds at this saving throw, both are unaffected.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/hellknight-dragoon-squad":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"notes":{"saves":"+2 circumstance bonus to saves vs fear effects","speed":"troop movement"},"flavor":"<p>Some fugitives are so dangerous or numerous that they warrant a whole Hellknight squadron who can ride after quarry and dismount to give chase in crowded settlements. These Hellknights wield flails as capably as they wield fear, using both to subdue and restrain foes.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"+2 Circumstance Bonus to Saves vs Fear Effects","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Bind Them in Chains","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature or troop adjacent to the dragoon squad gains the frightened condition, or an adjacent troop is reduced to 2 segments</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Sensing their foes' faltering morale, the dragoons lash out with their manacles. The triggering creature must attempt a DC 25 Reflex save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature becomes Clumsy 1 until the end of the squad's next turn.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature becomes Clumsy 2 until the end of the squad's next turn and is Immobilized until it Escapes.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but Restrained instead of immobilized.</p>"},{"n":"Break the Weak Link","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>10 feet.</p>\n<p>As long as the dragoon squad has at least 3 segments, all enemy troops within the aura take a –2 circumstance penalty to saves against emotion effects.</p>"},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Arrow Volley","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["magical"],"f":"","d":"<p>The dragoons draw bows and fire arrows as a ranged attack. This volley is a 10-foot burst within 80 feet that deals 4d8 piercing damage (DC 25 basic Reflex save). When the troop is reduced to 2 or fewer segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Fear the Chain","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The dragoons attempt to Demoralize all foes in a 15-foot emanation, comparing the result of a single Intimidation check to each target's Will DC. The squad doesn't take the penalty if they don't speak the same language as a target. It's possible for the dragoon squad to get a different degree of success for each target, and a target is temporarily immune to this ability only if the squad critically fails the check against them.</p>"},{"n":"Flail Assault","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["magical"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The dragoons lash out with their flails in a melee attack against each enemy in a 5-foot emanation (DC 25 basic Reflex save). The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 1d8+2 bludgeoning</p>\n<p>2 2d8+9 bludgeoning</p>\n<p>3 3d8+11 bludgeoning</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/hellknight-hunter-squad":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"lore":[["Monster Lore",29],["Warfare Lore",25]],"notes":{"saves":"+1 circumstance vs. emotion effects","speed":"troop movement"},"flavor":"<p>Against immense prey, Order of the Pike Hellknights assemble elite squads trained to strike as one, shield each other from fiery breath, protect civilians, and stand strong against foes that would terrify lesser troops.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"+1 Circumstance Bonus vs Emotion Effects","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Hunters of Monsters","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Hellknight hunters can use Monster Lore to Recall Knowledge about creatures of any type. Whenever one of the squad's damaging abilities would affect only a single creature that lacks the swarm or troop trait, they gain a +2 status bonus to that ability's Reflex save DC.</p>"},{"n":"Pin It Down","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An adjacent enemy uses a manipulate or move action, or leaves an adjacent space during a move action it's using</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The hunters stab with their longspears. The triggering enemy takes 4d8+9 piercing damage (DC 33 basic Reflex save). If the enemy critically fails this saving throw, the triggering action is disrupted.</p>"},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Disciplined Barricade","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Hellknights defensively lock their shields. Until the start of this troop's next turn, the troop and all allies within a 5-foot emanation gain a +1 circumstance bonus to their AC and Reflex saving throws.</p>"},{"n":"Hurl Javelins","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The squad's members throw a volley of javelins. Each creature in a 10-foot burst within 30 feet of the troop takes 5d6+9 piercing damage with a DC 33 basic Reflex save. When the Hellknight hunters are reduced to 2 segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Medic!","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["healing"],"f":"","d":"<p>The hunters bandage an adjacent creature. The target regains 5d8+20 healing Hit Points, after which the target is immune to this ability for 1 day.</p>"},{"n":"Phalanx Strike","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["magical"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The Hellknight hunters strike outward with their longspears in a uniform melee attack against each enemy in a 10-foot emanation (DC 33 basic Reflex save). The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 1d8+5 piercing damage</p>\n<p>2 4d8+9 piercing damage</p>\n<p>3 5d8+13 piercing damage</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/hellknight-paralictor":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"lore":[["Hell Lore",31]],"gear":["Mace","Steel Shield","Hellknight Plate"],"notes":{"ac":"(43 with shield raised)"},"focus":1,"abilities":[{"n":"Champion's Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>You're surrounded by an aura in a 15-foot emanation. It has the aura and divine traits. Any follower of your deity within the aura immediately knows you're a champion of your deity. This aura is used as the range for your champion's reaction and for various other effects. You can suppress or resume the aura as a single action, which has the concentrate trait, and it ends if you fall Unconscious.</p>"},{"n":"Exalted Iron Command","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy in your champion's aura damages you</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You put an impertinent foe who dared harm you in their proper place. You command each enemy in your champion's aura to kneel before you in obedience. If they dare to refuse, they must pay the price in pain and anguish. The enemy must choose one of the following options.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Kneel</strong> The enemy drops Prone as a free action.</p></li><li><p><strong>Refuse</strong> You deal 5d6 mental plus 5 persistent mental damage to the enemy.</p></li></ul><p>Regardless of which option the enemy chose, your Strikes against it deal 3 extra spirit damage until the end of your next turn.</p>\n<p>Effect: Champion's Extra Damage</p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Defensive Advance","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["flourish"],"f":"","d":"<p>With the protection of your shield, you dive into battle! You Raise your Shield and Stride. If you end your movement within melee reach of at least one enemy, you can make a melee Strike against that enemy.</p>\n<p>You can use Defensive Advance while Burrowing, Climbing, Flying, or Swimming instead of Striding if you have the corresponding movement type.</p>"},{"n":"Gruesome Strike","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Your Strikes currently deal extra damage from your champion's reaction.</p><hr><p>Make a Strike against the creature that triggered your champion's reaction. If you hit, double the extra damage the target takes from your reaction, and the target must succeed at a DC 40 Fortitude save or be Drained 1. Regardless of the result, the creature is temporarily immune to your Gruesome Strike for 24 hours.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/hellknight-sea-brigade":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"lore":[["Hell Lore",14]],"notes":{"hp":"troop defenses"},"flavor":"<p>A Hellknight cavalry brigade consists of several Hellknights and a single field-maralictor, all wearing the distinctive armor of their order and wielding lances. The maralictor speaks for the brigade, questioning travelers the brigade encounters and barking orders. A Hellknight brigade is typically based at a keep or other fortification controlling an area measured by a day's ride in every direction—about 25 miles. Farther-ranging missions are possible but require substantial logistical support.</p><hr><p>A military serves to defend and fight on behalf of nations and can be trained and deployed in various ways.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Thresholds</strong> 90 (3 segments), 45 (2 segments)</p>\n<hr>\n<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p>"},{"n":"Arrow Volley","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Hellknights draw or reload their longbows, then launch a ranged attack in the form of a volley. This volley is a 10-foot burst within 100 feet that deals 3d8+2 piercing damage (DC 23 basic Reflex save). When the troop is reduced to 2 or fewer segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Boarding Grapple","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The Hellknights are on a ship</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The Hellknights throw a volley of grappling hooks at a 10-foot-radius burst within 30 feet. Five grappling hooks landing at random squares in the burst take hold, and the Hellknights heave, forcibly moving both ships up to 15 feet toward each other until they're adjacent to each other. The ships remain adjacent to each other until all five of the grappling hooks are dislodged (each as an Interact action) or their respective chains are broken (Hardness 8, HP 20, BT 10).</p>"},{"n":"Sea Legs","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The ship crew ignores the penalty for attacking while on a vehicle that has moved in the last round and takes only a –2 penalty if the vehicle is uncontrolled or used an action with the reckless trait.</p>"},{"n":"Stab from the Saddle","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p>1 to 3</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The brigade engages in a coordinated lance attack against each enemy in a 10-foot emanation with a DC 25 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 1d6+7 piercing damage</p>\n<p>2 2d6+14 piercing damage</p>\n<p>3 3d6+18 piercing damage</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/house-thrune-elite-infantry":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"lore":[["Warfare Lore",27]],"notes":{"speed":"troop movement"},"abilities":[{"n":"Give No Ground","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>These soldiers have had it beaten into them that they shall hold their ground no matter what. If any effect would force the House Thrune elite infantry to move, reduce that distance by 10 feet. Any time it would be affected by the Fleeing condition, the elite infantry is instead Slowed 2 for the same duration.</p>"},{"n":"Hell's Will","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>As long as it has 4 segments, the House Thrune elite infantry troop improves its degree of success on rout checks by one step, even when without a commander. When it has three segments, it instead gains a +2 status bonus to rout checks.</p>"},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Cloven Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The House Thrune elite infantry charges forward with an infernal yell on cloven hooves. The troop Strides up to twice its Speed. At the end of the troop's movement, each enemy within a 10-foot emanation takes 2d6+7 piercing damage with a DC 34 basic Reflex save.</p>"},{"n":"Crossbow Array","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The House Thrune elite infantry unit draws, loads, and fires a barrage from its crossbows. The salvo is a 10-foot burst within 100 feet that deals 5d8 piercing damage (DC 34 basic Reflex save). When the elite infantry is reduced to 2 segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Hellish Spears","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The House Thrune elite infantry attacks each enemy in a 10-foot emanation with its flaming longspears, with a DC 34 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 2d6+2 piercing damage plus 1d6 fire damage</p>\n<p>2 4d6+7 piercing damage plus 1d6 fire damage</p>\n<p>3 7d6+10 piercing damage plus 1d6 fire damage</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/ignaro-vollai":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Fey"],"lore":[["Devil Lore",26]],"gear":["Staff of Control","+1 Dottari Robes","Manacles (Average) (5)","Precious Metals","Material Component Pouch"],"abilities":[{"n":"Hell's Arrest","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack","magical","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Ignaro invokes Hell to wrap in chains a creature within 30 feet of him. He attempts to Grapple the target using his Arcana modifier in place of Athletics for the check. If successful, the chains keep the target grappled or Restrained for 1 minute, until the target Escapes, or until the chains are destroyed (Hardness 10, 30 HP), whichever comes first.</p>"},{"n":"Hell's Own Servitor","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Ignaro is bound to a phistophilus in Erebus. When Ignaro dies, his body disintegrates and his soul is sent to Hell. All weapons that he wields deal an additional 1d6 spirit damage with the unholy trait.</p>"},{"n":"Ignite Heresy","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine","fire","magical","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>Ignaro declares an object he can see within 30 feet to be heretical. After smoldering for 1 round, it's engulfed in flames, taking 3d6 persistent fire damage that ignores half of the object's Hardness. Immersion in water for 1 round ends the damage, as does the object being splashed with a flask of holy water. Any other water effect that isn't just mundane water used against the object can attempt to counteract the effect (DC 30). If this ability destroys an object, Ignaro gains temporary Hit Points equal to twice the object's level (minimum 2) that last for 1 minute.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/infernal-bow-shocks":{"description":"<p>Wave after wave of Hellish power ripples out from the pentagram surrounding the Inferno Gate, bathing all of the battling armies around it in its dark energies. Some are slain on the spot, while others fall into cracks that open beneath them in the earth, and still others are consumed by ignited gasses.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 34 Devil Lore or DC 34 Hell Lore to give the proper incantations and invoke the name of Visperthul to ward off the magical defenses from the Inferno Gate; DC 38 Arcana (expert), DC 38 Nature (expert), DC 38 Occultism (expert), or DC 38 Religion (expert) to erect a magical barrier to shield against the power emanating from the gate; DC 43 Survival to use the natural terrain as a shield to survive the onslaught of magical energies; DC 48 Will save to simply push back against the Hellish storm surge and refute them; or Dispel Magic (9th rank; counteract DC 34) to blast the bow shock with magic to stem its flow; three successes are required to dissipate the hazard's energies.</p><p>The first time a PC successfully uses Devil Lore or Hell Lore against this hazard, all PCs gain a +2 status bonus to their saving throws against the hazard's effects.</p>","routine":"<p>(2 actions) The infernal bow shocks release a different effect each round for 3 rounds, centered on a randomly-chosen PC each time and never the same PC twice in a row (though creatures standing near each other might just be unlucky). In the first round, it unleashes Flaming Fumes. In the second round, it uses an 8th-rank whispers of the void spell (DC 38), and in the third round, it emulates the effect of an earthquake spell (DC 38), with each of the three piles of tower rubble collapsing as though they were shoddy structures. Notably, no fissures extend into the former inner bailey of Fort Arego (area <strong>E4</strong>, as outlined by the remaining rectangular battlements). The hazard concludes for the PCs when it's disabled, or when the third round ends.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Shock Wave","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Encounter <strong>E3</strong> begins</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> A randomly chosen PC is targeted at the center of a 20-foot burst of acrid-smelling (but invisible) fumes. The hazard unleashes Flaming Fumes on the same target as Shock Wave. A creature must succeed at a Perception check against the hazard's Stealth DC to visually detect the fumes. The infernal bow shocks then roll initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Flaming Fumes","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>A 20-foot burst of acrid-smelling fumes ignites in gouts of hellfire. All creatures in the area take 7d6 fire plus 7d6 spirit damage with a DC 38 basic Reflex save.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/infernal-tide":{"lang":["Diabolic","Empyrean","telepathy 100 feet"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","speed":"troop movement"},"flavor":"<p>Sarglagons can gather to form an infernal tide, a troop that displays unnerving fluidity in the way its devils seem to flow around each other.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"At-Will Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster can cast its at-will spells any number of times without using up spell slots.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Heavy Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","incapacitation"],"f":"","d":"<p>10 feet.</p>\n<p>A creature that enters the aura becomes Encumbered while it remains in the aura unless it succeeds at a DC 30 Will save, after which it's immune for 10 minutes.</p>"},{"n":"Stygian Guardian","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature or object within 5 feet of the troop is targeted by an attack or offensive troop ability</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Some of the infernal tide interpose themselves, giving the target standard cover against the attack, or greater cover if the troop was already granting it lesser cover.</p>"},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Drown","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","incapacitation","water"],"f":"","d":"<p>The infernal tide conjures murky water to fill the lungs of all creatures that can't breathe water within a 30-foot cone. Each target in the area must attempt a DC 30 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target coughs up water and becomes Sickened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target must hold its breath. The only action it can take is to attempt a DC 30 Fortitude save to expel the water, which is a single action.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target falls Unconscious and begins suffocating. If the target succeeds at its Fortitude save while suffocating, it coughs up the water and can breathe again.</p>"},{"n":"Sarglagon Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 33 Fortitude</p><hr><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 3d6 poison damage and Clumsy 1 (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 4d6 poison damage and Clumsy 2 (1 round)</p>"},{"n":"Tentacle Onslaught","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["magical","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The troop lashes out their tentacles in a coordinated melee attack against each enemy in a 5-foot emanation (DC 30 basic Reflex save). The damage depends on the number of actions. A creature that fails its save is also exposed to sarglagon venom.</p>\n<p>1 1d8+3 bludgeoning damage</p>\n<p>2 4d8+6 bludgeoning damage</p>\n<p>3 5d8+10 bludgeoning damage</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/kaisentia":{"lang":["Azlanti","Common"],"lore":[["Tailoring Lore",35]],"gear":["Explorer's Clothing","Tailoring Toolkit (Sterling)","Crown of Intellect","Key"],"abilities":[{"n":"Search Your Mind","a":"1","c":"interaction","t":["concentrate"],"f":"once per hour","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You gain the effects of Hypercognition.</p>"},{"n":"Sartorial Snag","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An adjacent creature uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The disciple drives several threaded needles through the triggering creature's clothing and pulls, momentarily binding its outfit and restricting movement. The disciple attempts a Tailoring Lore check against the triggering creature's AC. If the triggering creature isn't wearing at least a cloak, sash, tabard, or similar amount of visible cloth, apply a –2 circumstance penalty to this check.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> As success, plus the disciple disrupts the action.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> Threads partly entangle the triggering creature, it becomes Clumsy 1 and takes a –10-foot circumstance penalty to it Speeds until the beginning of its next turn. Any creature within reach of the targeted creature can end these effects with an Interact action.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The triggering creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The disciple becomes Off-Guard until the beginning of their next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Sequester","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"once per hour","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Kaisentia instantly transports herself and any items she's carrying to area <strong>B9</strong>, as if casting Translocate as a 9th-rank spell with a maximum range of 5 miles.</p>"},{"n":"Pins and Needles","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The disciple gains access to the critical specialization effects of their sleeve and needle Strikes, with a DC of 34.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The disciple's Strikes deal an additional 2d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Tailor-Made Armaments","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>While wearing clothing worth at least 10 gp, a disciple of thread can cause their sleeves or other parts of their outfit to extend and animate as unarmed Strikes in the flail weapon group. While wielding these sleeves, the cultist can use their Tailoring Lore modifier in place of Athletics to Grapple, Reposition, and Trip. As a free action while carrying a tailoring toolkit, the disciple can Draw mundane sewing needles to use as lethal throwing weapons in the bow weapon group.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/liabriz-corborra":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Dwarven"],"gear":["Warhammer (Shattered)","Mace","Steel Shield","Hellknight Breastplate","Religious Symbol of Asmodeus"],"focus":2,"abilities":[{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Torag's Apostate","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Liabriz only recently forswore Torag. While he carries his shattered warhammer, he gains a +1 status bonus on saves versus Torag and those that gain divine power from him. If Liabriz fails a save against Torag or one of his servitors, Liabriz critically fails instead.</p>"},{"n":"Channeling Block","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When Liabriz Shield Blocks, he can expend a Harm spell. He rolls 6d8 and increases his shield's Hardness by that total for the block.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/majordomo-cizoboseth":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Empyrean","Telepathy 100 feet"],"lore":[["Heraldry Lore",32]],"flavor":"<p>Where a bright mind seeking knowledge becomes corrupted by eloquent lies and twisted truths, an ayngavhaul is sure to lurk. Often donned in the holy vestments of other faiths in a twisted mockery of their principles, these wily, well-read devils delight in using their knowledge to twist religious texts and teachings into the dangerous principles those same texts warn against. While many ayngavhauls develop advanced knowledge of unique specializations, there are many whose depth of knowledge of a single religion rivals that of even the most wizened priests.</p>\n<p>Any information an ayngavhaul has read or learned is added to a massive living tome unique to the ayngavhaul. The information contained sorts itself based on the topic and point its owner is making.</p>\n<p>While these devils spend most of their time in the libraries of Hell, they are most often summoned in desperate bids by students seeking lost or forbidden knowledge, and such knowledge comes with a cost. These devils use truths and loose interpretations of texts to lend credence to their heretical viewpoints. When these once-bright intellectuals are corrupted into blasphemous priests, tyrants, and despots spreading the twisted words of an ayngavhaul, that devil gains influence and renown within the scholarly circles of Hell.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"Personal Archive","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Cizoboseth keeps records of palace events and accounts in a personal archive, a floating collection of ledgers constantly revolving around him. Retrieving or returning a ledger requires an Interact action.</p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Spellblock Ledger","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["divine","manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Cizoboseth is targeted by a spell</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Cizoboseth flings a ledger from his personal archive at the spell. He attempts a DC 5 Flat. On a success, the ledger fully absorbs the effects of the spell and burns up into a harmless pile of ash. Regardless of the result, Cizoboseth can't use this ability again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Herald Heresy","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","divine","mental","spirit","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>Cizoboseth imparts blasphemous thoughts into the minds of all non-devil creatures within a 20-foot burst up to 60 feet away. An affected creature takes 3d10 mental damage plus 3d10 spirit damage and must attempt a DC 37 Will save. Affected creatures gain a cumulative +1 circumstance bonus (up to a total of +4) to saves against all future attempts to Herald Heresy for 1 minute, as they become inured to the blasphemies.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and becomes temporarily immune for 1 hour.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and becomes Slowed 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage and becomes Slowed 2.</p>"},{"n":"Poison Minds","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Creatures hit by Cizoboseth's searing words must succeed at a DC 37 Will saving throw or become Stupefied 1 for 1 round (Stupefied 2 on a critical failure). If the target is trained in Religion, it takes a –2 circumstance penalty to its save.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/marala":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Fey","Strix"],"gear":["+2 Greater Striking Corundum (High-Grade ) Flail","Corundum (High-Grade) Shield","Explorer's Clothing","Silver Chunk"],"abilities":[{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Extol","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>Marala hefts her shield and orders a strix ally to protect themselves as well. Marala Raises a Shield, then causes one other strix ally within 30 feet to also Raise a Shield as a free action.</p>"},{"n":"Glorify","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Marala invokes the valor of her strix allies. Up to four strix allies within 30 feet can Step, Stride, or Fly up to their Speed toward an enemy as a free action. If she used 2 actions to activate this ability, up to two of the affected strix of Marala's choice can then Strike an adjacent enemy as a reaction.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/mareshiah":{"lang":["Aklo","Chthonian","Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Empyrean","Sakvroth","telepathy 100 feet, truespeech"],"lore":[["Legal Lore",41]],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"abilities":[{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"At-Will Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster can cast its at-will spells any number of times without using up spell slots.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Ward Contract","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A signed contract carried by Mareshiah (including draped over her horns) is immune to damage from all creatures other than her. Mareshiah is immune to mental effects that would make them destroy, nullify, or alter a contract.</p>"},{"n":"Draft Contract","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["divine","manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>Mareshiah produces an infernal contract for a single living mortal. This contract can grant a wide range of abilities and effects, akin to the power of a wish ritual but fulfilled to the letter by Mareshiah. To receive any of those benefits, the mortal must willingly sign their true name to the contract. At that point, the mortal's soul is bound to Mareshiah and Hell.</p>\n<p>While the contract is in effect, the victim can't be restored to life except by a wish ritual or similar magic. If the mortal is restored to life by those means, Mareshiah knows which mortal came to life and can locate the creature or creatures who restored the mortal to life for 1 year, gaining the effects of a pinpoint spell. Avoiding the terms of an infernal contract is difficult and often dangerous.</p>"},{"n":"Greater Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>3d6+15 bludgeoning, DC 42 basic Fortitude</p>\n<p>Only when grabbed by Binding Contract</p><hr><p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC. A creature that fails this save falls Unconscious, and a creature that succeeds is then temporarily immune to falling unconscious from Greater Constrict for 1 minute.</p></p>"},{"n":"Infernal Investment","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Mareshiah can cast a 10th-rank innate Scrying spell at will, but only to target a creature with which they have a contract. The target automatically critically fails its save.</p>"},{"n":"Infernal Wound","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The wounds from Mareshiah's Strikes resist healing.</p>\n<p>A spellcaster or item attempting to use healing magic on a creature damaged by Mareshiah's Strikes must first attempt to counteract infernal wound (DC 42). If it isn't counteracted, the healing has no effect.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/meliar-aructus":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","truespeech"],"lore":[["Hell Lore",33]],"gear":["Mace","Explorer's Clothing"],"abilities":[{"n":"At-Will Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster can cast its at-will spells any number of times without using up spell slots.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Contractual Lifespan","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>Meliar Aructus takes 25 untyped damage at the end of his turn if he Cast a Spell, used Borrow Time, or made a Strike that turn. This damage ignores resistance.</p>"},{"n":"Infernal Tendrils","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet.</p>\n<p>When a creature in the aura would be healed by a vitality effect, the healing is reduced by 15, and Meliar Aructus regains 15 healing Hit Points.</p>"},{"n":"Mark of the Devil","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["curse","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>Whoever kills Meliar must succeed at a DC 35 Will save or be visibly marked as anathema to Asmodeus. They gain weakness 10 to unholy damage and take a –2 circumstance penalty to Charisma-based skill checks against followers of Asmodeus. The DCs of checks to Gather information about or Track the marked creature are reduced by 2. The mark can't be hidden.</p>"},{"n":"Shattered Vessel","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine","spirit","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>When Meliar dies, the divine power barely contained within his body explodes outward, dealing 6d8 spirit damage to each creature in a 30-foot emanation (DC 33 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Borrow Time","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["divine","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>Meliar chooses two different creatures in his infernal tendrils aura. Each one must be either a devil or himself. One target loses 25 HP, and the other regains that many HP. Unwilling targets can negate the transfer with a successful DC 39 Fortitude save.</p>"},{"n":"Chill of Cocytus","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>Meliar's unarmed attacks and mace gain the +2 greater striking decaying frost runes when used by him, and his Strikes gain the death trait.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/merztorlegon":{"lore":[["Warfare Lore",37]],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"flavor":"<p>Merztorlegons are walking siege engines, their bodies bristling with ballistae and siege towers bolted to their shoulders. Their frontal armor leaves their back less defended, forcing Hell's commanders to support these juggernauts with infantry that can shield them from flanking strikes.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Arrow Volley","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["magical","unholy"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The vordines fire projectiles, dealing 7d8 piercing damage to creatures in a 10-foot burst within 200 feet (DC 38 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Besieging Fury","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A merztorlegon and their crew can Demoralize creatures at a range of 120 feet and don't take a penalty for not sharing a language with the target.</p>"},{"n":"Shoulder Ballista","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A shoulder ballista is an extension of the merztorlegon's body, functioning as a siege weapon that shares the demon's space, can't be targeted, and ceases to function after the merztorlegon's death. Either the merztorlegon or their siege crew can Aim or Load the ballista, but only the crew can Launch it.</p>\n<p><strong>Aim</strong> 1 80 feet, minimum distance 30 feet</p>\n<p><strong>Load</strong> 1 (manipulate) 1 time</p>\n<p><strong>Launch</strong> 1 (attack, magical, manipulate, range increment 120 feet, unholy) 8d12 piercing, single target, DC 41 Reflex</p>"},{"n":"Siege Crew","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Several vordines inhabit the siege tower and are an extension of the merztorlegon, use the devil's skill modifiers, and can't be targeted individually. On the siege devil's turn, the crew can take 2 actions that can be used only to launch an Arrow Volley; Demoralize; or to Aim, Load, or Launch the devil's shoulder ballista. Once the merztorlegon is reduced to half their maximum Hit Points, the siege crew is injured and takes only 1 action per turn.</p>"},{"n":"Sunder Structures","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A merztorlegon's melee Strikes deal an additional 3d12 untyped damage to items and structures.</p>"},{"n":"Troop Transport","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The merztorlegon gathers a willing adjacent troop into their siege tower or shunts a stored troop into an adjacent space. The devil can store only one troop at a time, during which time the troop can't take actions, can't be targeted by effects, can be transported by the devil's translocate spell, and increases the damage dealt by Arrow Volley by 2d8. If the merztorlegon is defeated, any stored troop immediately reappears in or adjacent to the siege devil's space.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Knockdown","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Knockdown in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Trip the creature as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty.</p></p>"},{"n":"Improved Push","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Push in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Shove the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty. If Improved Push lists a distance, change the distance the creature is pushed on a success to that distance.</p></p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Siege Hammer":"<p>Improved Knockdown or Improved Push</p>"}},"hells-destiny-bestiary/murderous-mannequin":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Elven","Empyrean","Fey","Jotun"],"abilities":[{"n":"Dance Partner","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An adjacent creature whom the mannequin dealt damage to with a fist Strike since the beginning of the mannequin's last turn attempts to move away from the mannequin</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The mannequin dances after the triggering creature, either Climbing or Striding, following the creature and staying in reach throughout its movement until the creature stops moving or the mannequin has moved up to its full Speed, whichever happens first. The mannequin gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC and Reflex saves against reactions triggered by its movement. If it critically succeeds at a Reflex save against a reaction triggered by its movement (or if the attacker critically fails its attack roll or check), the mannequin maneuvers the creature it's following so that the latter is exposed to the reaction; the attacker rerolls the attack roll or check against the followed creature or forces the followed creature to attempt a Reflex save against the reaction instead.</p>"},{"n":"Accessorized","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The mannequin wears accessories (typically three) that it can Draw as a free action and use as thrown weapons. The type of damage varies by the accessory, such as slashing damage for a wide-brimmed hat, piercing for a stiletto-heeled shoe, or bludgeoning for a handbag.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Accessory":"<p>Damage type depends on object thrown</p>"}},"hells-destiny-bestiary/nemyra":{"lang":["Common","Elven","Fey","Muan"],"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>Also called a hamadryad, a dryad queen rules over an entire forest, or a portion of an incredibly large forest, leading and protecting all dryads within. Dryad queens often have strange relationships with powerful and deadly fey, working together in a dualistic way despite their differences, with the queen representing nature's wonders and the other fey representing nature's wrath.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Nymphs are a family of fey that take the form of beautiful humanoids with elven features and have a deep association with the natural world. The most common of their kind are the dryads, which are spirits that embody great trees, but many other kinds of nymphs exist, including naiads, who watch over bodies of water. All nymphs are guardians of some element of nature, typically a specific tree or pond, or even-in the case of nymph queens-whole forests or massive bodies of water</p>\n<h2>Nymph Queens</h2>\n<p>Nymph queens are powerful nymphs who rule over entire regions of untouched wilderness, not just single trees or ponds. Every variety of nymph can have a queen. Naiad queens are among the most prominent, and more often interact with nearby mortals. Thus, some scholars refer to naiad queens as simply \"nymphs.\"</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Nature Empathy","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The dryad can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals and plants.</p>"},{"n":"Tied to the Sea","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Nemyra is tied to the kelp forest in this room and treats the kelp as a tree for the purposes of her spells and abilities. Creatures that she summons with her Summon Plant or Fungus spell have the aquatic trait and a swim speed of 30 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Nymph's Beauty","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","emotion","mental","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. On a failed save, the target is Immobilized in awe for 1 minute.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Creatures that start their turn in the aura must succeed at a DC 30 Will save or suffer an effect described in the nymph queen's entry.</p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["polymorph","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>Nymph queens can transform between their original form, which looks much like a typical nymph of their kind, and any Small or Medium humanoid form, typically choosing a more humanoid-looking version of their natural form.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"Focus Beauty","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>On a failed save, if the target was already affected by the dryad queen's beauty, the target can't use hostile actions against the dryad queen for 1 hour.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>The nymph queen focuses her beauty upon a target, who must attempt a save against her nymph's beauty aura (DC 30 Will save). If the creature fails and was already affected by the aura, it takes a greater effect described in the nymph queen's entry.</p>\n<p>A nymph queen can Focus Beauty on a given creature only once per turn.</p>"},{"n":"Inspiration","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The nymph queen inspires a single intelligent creature by giving that creature a token of her favor, typically a lock of her hair, though it can be some other significant object as well. As long as the creature carries her token and remains in good standing with her, the creature gains a +1 status bonus to all Crafting checks, Performance checks, and Will saves.</p>\n<p>If the nymph grants her token to a bard, and she's the bard's muse, the queen chooses one additional benefit granted by her token: a +1 status bonus to all Lore checks, a +2 status bonus to Performance checks when determining the effects of compositions, a +4 status bonus to untrained skill checks, or a +2 status bonus to Will saves against fey.</p>\n<p>Effect: Nymph Queen's Inspiration</p>"},{"n":"Tree Meld","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>A One with Plants spell cast by a dryad has an unlimited duration.</p>\n<p>In addition, if the dryad merges with any tree in her domain, she can choose to instead enter an extradimensional living space within the tree, and can bring up to eight adjacent, willing creatures with her; the spell gains the extradimensional trait. The dryad can still be expelled from this space.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/nyvorlas-yandor":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Sailing Lore",13]],"gear":["Dagger (4)","Rapier","Studded Leather Armor"],"flavor":"<p>Whenever high command needs an enemy spellcaster taken off the board in the midst of battle, they send in a mage killer.</p><hr><p>Whether they're hired to wage war, protect a caravan, or infiltrate an impenetrable fortress, there's ample work for mercenaries all over Golarion.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Spell Dodge","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The mage killer is targeted by a spell</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The mage killer gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC and saving throws against the triggering spell.</p>"},{"n":"Spell Interception","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 10 feet of the mage killer Casts a Spell</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The mage killer makes a melee Strike or thrown dagger Strike against the triggering creature. If it hits, the spell is disrupted.</p>"},{"n":"Magical Static","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["arcane","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The mage killer's Strikes deal an additional 1d8+2 mental damage to a creature that has Cast (or attempted to Cast) a Spell within the last round, and on a critical hit, the creature is Stupefied 1 for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Shift Energy Runes","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","concentrate"],"f":"once per hour","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The mage killer alters the magical countermeasures in the runes on their armor. They change their resistance to the energy type of their choice (acid, cold, electricity, fire, force, sonic, vitality, or void).</p>"},{"n":"Squad's Spell Dodge","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When Nyvorlas uses her Spell Dodge reaction, any troop she commands also gains the saving throw bonus against the triggering spell.</p>"},{"n":"Squad's Static","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Any troop Nyvorlas commands also gains her magical static ability, applying its effects to her troop's offensive abilities.</p>"},{"n":"Sudden Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The mage killer Strides twice. If they end their movement within melee reach of at least one enemy, they can make a melee Strike against it.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/oath-howler":{"lang":["Sussuran","oathsense"],"notes":{"saves":"+2 status to all saves vs. auditory and sonic","per":"oathsense","speed":"swiftness"},"flavor":"<p>Sometimes the wind catches a profane oath as it's uttered, carrying it far away before the blasphemy can form a tortured eddy that repeats the curse again and again. Such winds eventually tie themselves in a knot and take on a sinister intelligence.</p>\n<p>The unholy negotiations Abrogail I held with Hell deep in the Whisperwood spun off an untold number of oath howlers, most of whom haunt that forest and its skies to this day. Oath howlers delight in other creatures' profanities. A potential victim can distract the elementals indefinitely so long as the speaker varies their languages, insults, and intonation. If done artfully, a creature might sandwich a request between pejoratives and so earn an oath howler's morbid cooperation—at least so long as they continue encouraging the elemental with fresh profane oaths.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Oathsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The oath howler can hear profanities—anything from foul language to someone casting an unholy spell that lacks the subtle trait—uttered within 1 mile, after which they can detect the speaker as a vague sense for 1 minute (or as an imprecise sense within 100 feet). The oath howler can understand profanities in any language, including several words that precede and follow the profanity for context, and thereafter can mimic and repeat those profanities.</p>"},{"n":"+2 Status to All Saves vs. Auditory and Sonic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Rebuking Smoke","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["air"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 30 feet damages the oath howler</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The oath howler's wound belches foul smoke onto the triggering creature, who must attempt a DC 30 Fortitude save. The creature is then immune to that oath howler's Rebuking Smoke for 1 minute.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Dazzled for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is dazzled for 1 round and Sickened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is sickened 1 and Blinded until the sickened condition ends.</p>"},{"n":"Storm of Blasphemies","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["sonic","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>The oath howler roars in a 30-foot cone, shouting dozens of pejoratives in as many languages. Creatures in the area take 10d8 sonic damage (DC 33 basic Fortitude save). Creatures that critically fail also take 2d8 persistent sonic damage and are Deafened until the persistent damage ends.</p>\n<p>The oath howler can't use this ability again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Swiftness","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The oath howler's movement doesn't trigger reactions.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/obrimar":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"gear":["Crossbow","Mace","Steel Shield","Full Plate","Religious Symbol (Silver)"],"focus":2,"abilities":[{"n":"Unholy Shield","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>In Obrimar's hands, his shield gains the <em>moderate reinforcing</em> rune, giving it Hardness 8, 84 HP, and BT 42.</p>"},{"n":"Champion's Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>15 feet.</p>\n<p>Any follower of Asmodeus in the aura knows Obrimar is a champion of Asmodeus. At the end of Obrimar's turn, each ally in the aura reduces their frightened value by 1. The aura can be suppressed or resumed with a single action, which has the concentrate trait, and ends if Obrimar falls Unconscious.</p>"},{"n":"Exalted Iron Command","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy in Obrimar's champion's aura damages him</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The creature that damaged Obrimar can choose to drop Prone as a free action. If it refuses, it takes 4d6 mental damage and 4 persistent spirit damage. All other enemies within Obrimar's champion's aura must also drop prone as a free action or else take 4 mental damage if they refuse.</p>"},{"n":"Infernal Courage","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When Obrimar becomes frightened, he reduces the condition value by 1 (to a minimum of 0).</p>"},{"n":"Infernal Reactions","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>At the start of each of his turns, Obrimar gains an additional reaction that he can only use to make a Reactive Strike or Shield Block.</p>"},{"n":"Never Fall","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Obrimar's Hit Points are reduced to 0 for the first time that day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Obrimar refuses to give up his soul to Asmodeus just yet. He remains standing with 25 healing Hit Points.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Never Falter","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Obrimar declares his devotion to Asmodeus and the cause of obedience. He Strides, then makes a melee Strike. If the Strike hits an enemy, all allies within his champion's aura gain a +2 status bonus to attack rolls and saving throws against fear until the start of Obrimar's next turn.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/ochiastis":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","telepathy 100 feet"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"flavor":"<p>While Hell prefers to subjugate mortals by force, cow them with majesty, or bind them through contracts, even the most principled archdevil sometimes needs an assassin. In their natural form, an ochiastis resembles a nephilim with a narrow mane of venomous quills running from the top of their head to the small of their back. This fiend is a capable shapeshifter, yet their quills remain no matter the shape they take—a drawback an ochiastis tries to keep hidden by wearing a cloak or other bulky clothing. When not on missions, an ochiastis often lurks in urban areas, familiarizing themself with local behaviors and shortcuts.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Assassin's Pursuit","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The ochiastis's hunted prey is within their reach and attempts to move away from them</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ochiastis Climbs or Strides up to their Speed, following their hunted prey and keeping it in reach throughout its movement until it stops moving or the ochiastis has moved their full Speed.</p>"},{"n":"Faceless Escape","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["move"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The ochiastis takes damage</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The ochiastis is in or adjacent to a crowd of at least 10 people</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ochiastis attempts to Hide by blending into the crowd, even if the devil lacks cover or concealment. The ochiastis can then Sneak. Each time the ochiastis becomes hidden from a creature in this way, that creature gains a cumulative +2 circumstance bonus to its Perception DC for 1 hour against the ochiastis's Stealth checks when using Faceless Escape.</p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p>The ochiastis can take the appearance of any Small or Medium humanoid creature. This doesn't change the ochiastis's Speed or their attack and damage bonuses with their claw Strike but might change the damage type this Strike deals (typically to bludgeoning). They lose their quill Strike. Creatures that Grapple the ochiastis or otherwise touch their back gain a +4 circumstance bonus to see through their disguise.</p><hr><p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"Hunt Prey","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>You designate a single creature as your prey and focus your attacks against that creature. You must be able to see or hear the prey, or you must be tracking the prey during exploration.</p>\n<p>You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks when you Seek your prey and a +2 circumstance bonus to Survival checks when you Track your prey. You also ignore the penalty for making ranged attacks within your second range increment against the prey you're hunting.</p>\n<p>You can have only one creature designated as your prey at a time. If you use Hunt Prey against a creature when you already have a creature designated, the prior creature loses the designation and the new prey gains the designation. Your designation lasts until your next daily preparations.</p>"},{"n":"Ochiastis Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison","virulent"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 36 Fortitude</p><hr><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Enfeebled 1 and Off-Guard (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Enfeebled 2 and off-guard (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> enfeebled 2, off-guard, and Slowed 1 (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 4</strong> Enfeebled 3 and Paralyzed (1 round)</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The creature's Strikes deal an additional 3d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/oourax":{"lang":["Common","Cyclops","Jistkan","Jotun"],"lore":[["Fortune-Telling Lore",27],["Hell Lore",27]],"gear":["Greataxe","Hide Armor","Eternal Eruption of Droskar's Crag"],"abilities":[{"n":"Doorway Traveler","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Oourax has journeyed through 13 red-tinged doorways in Narona and drawn power from them, granting her 130 temporary Hit Points for 1 week. For each Narona doorway that the PCs have sealed, reduce this amount by 10.</p>"},{"n":"Ferocity","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster is reduced to 0 HP.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster avoids being knocked out and remains at 1 HP, but its Wounded value increases by 1. When it is Wounded 3, it can no longer use this ability</p></p>"},{"n":"Flash of Insight","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":["fortune","occult"],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Oourax is about to roll a d20</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Oourax peers into an occluded spectrum of possible futures. She gets a success (but not a critical success) on the roll instead of rolling.</p>"},{"n":"Hellfire Magic","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":["spellshape","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>Oourax can shape her spells into hellfire. Whenever she casts chain lightning, fireball, ignition, or wall of fire, instead of its normal damage, she can have the spell deal half its damage as fire damage and half as spirit damage.</p>"},{"n":"Lava Bomb","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>You fling the <em>eternal eruption</em>, with the effect of <em>Frozen Lava of Droskar's Crag</em>. After 2d4 hours, the <em>eternal eruption</em> reforms itself in a container on your person, typically the one you most recently stored it in.</p><hr><p><em>Eternal Eruption of Droskar's Crag</em> deals 13d6 fire on a DC 32 basic Reflex.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/page-and-chapter":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Draconic"],"lore":[["Library Lore",32],["Scribing Lore",32]],"notes":{"saves":"+2 status to all saves vs. linguistic effects"},"abilities":[{"n":"Mage Bond","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>After performing a 1-hour ritual, a scalescribe can bond with one willing creature capable of Casting Spells. The scalescribe can Aid their bonded caster in Crafting a scroll, and they can make their Transcribed spell available to the caster so long as the spell is of the caster's tradition. A bonded prepared caster can prepare the spell. A bonded spontaneous caster can add the spell to their spell repertoire during their daily preparations, and it remains as long as the Transcribed scroll exists.</p>"},{"n":"+2 Status to All Saves vs. Linguistic Effects","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Transcribe","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Another creature targets the scalescribe with a spell requiring verbal components</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The scalescribe attempts to copy the incantation onto a scroll by attempting a counteract check (counteract rank 8, counteract modifier +28) with the following effects instead of the normal effects of counteracting. The spell still affects the scalescribe, regardless of the results of this check. The scalescribe can Cast a Spell from any scroll they Transcribe as if it were on their spell list. Transcribing a new scroll renders any previously Transcribed scroll inert.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> If the triggering spell's rank was no more than 2 higher than the scalescribe's counteract rank, the scalescribe captures a copy of the spell in a scroll that appears in their hand. This scroll can be used normally but fades after 24 hours if not used before then.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> As critical success, but only if the spell's rank is no more than 1 higher than the scalescribe's counteract rank.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> As critical success, but only if the spell's rank is lower than the scalescribe's counteract rank.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The scalescribe fails to copy the spell.</p>"},{"n":"Inkstain","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the scalescribe deals damage to a creature with their fountain pen, the creature takes 4d4 persistent poison damage. When a creature taking this damage attempts to take an action with the concentrate trait, it must succeed at a DC 5 Flat or the action is disrupted.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/pain-coral":{"description":"<p>Haunted coral transfers pain between creatures.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 33 Nature or DC 37 Occultism or DC 37 Thievery to pinpoint and disable key synaptic nerves throughout the coral, DC 37 Religion to quell the coral's tortured memories; each success reduces the coral's number of actions per turn by 1, and the hazard is disabled when after four successes.</p>","reset":"<p>The coral diffuses and resets after 1 minute.</p>","routine":"<p>(4 actions) The coral casts Phantom Pain as a 6th-rank spell on a target (DC 33), targeting creatures that aren't already taking persistent mental damage.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Surge of Pain","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature takes damage within area <strong>D4</strong></p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The brain coral casts Spirit Link on Xendra. The hazard rolls initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Share the Sadism","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 30 feet of the coral takes persistent mental damage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The coral grants an equal number of temporary Hit Points to a different creature within 30 feet.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/palace-guard":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"lore":[["Legal Lore",25]],"gear":["Crossbow","Mace","Sturdy Shield (Greater)","Breastplate"],"notes":{"ac":" (38 with shield raised)"},"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Hellish Determination","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The palace guard's training allows them to shrug off debilitating effects. The palace guard chooses a nonpermanent condition affecting them. That condition ends. This doesn't heal any Hit Points already lost from the condition, and it can't remove conditions occurring automatically due to the palace guard's situation or positioning (such as Prone or flanked).</p>"},{"n":"Vicious Swing","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["flourish"],"f":"","d":"<p>The palace guard makes a melee Strike. This counts as two attacks for the palace guard's multiple attack penalty. If this Strike hits, they deal two extra dice of weapon damage.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/pure-legion-squad":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Warfare Lore",24]],"notes":{"speed":"troop movement"},"flavor":"<p>Soldiers who participate in multiple campaigns of war gain the experience necessary to become their military's finest fighting forces. First-class infantry troops are deployed on battlefields where winning the day is of the utmost importance.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Cloak of Purity","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Pure Legion receives a +2 circumstance bonus to saves against spells and effects with the divine, holy, or unholy traits. If commanded by a character who can cast divine spells, the Pure Legion squad takes a –2 circumstance penalty to all rout checks.</p>"},{"n":"No Retreat","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>These soldiers have been extensively trained to hold their ground no matter the situation. If any effect would force the pure legion squad to move, reduce the distance by 10 feet. Any time they would be affected by the Fleeing condition, the pure legion squad is instead Slowed 2 for the same duration.</p>"},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>HP</strong> 240 (4 segments); <strong>Thresholds</strong> 160 (3 segments), 80 (2 segments)</p>\n<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Bolt Salvo","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The pure legion squad draws, loads, and shoots a salvo from their crossbows. The salvo is a 10-foot burst within 120 feet that deals 4d8 piercing damage (DC 30 basic Reflex save). When the pure legion squad is reduced to 2 segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Clash of Steel","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p>1 to 3</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The pure legion squad attacks each enemy in a 5-foot emanation, with a DC 29 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 2d6+1 slashing damage</p>\n<p>2 4d6+10 slashing damage</p>\n<p>3 4d6+18 slashing damage</p>"},{"n":"Drilled in Formations","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The pure legion squad uses Change Formation. A pure legion squad unit typically knows the marching column and wedge formations.</p>"},{"n":"First-class Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The pure legion squad rushes forward with a hunger for battle. They Stride up to twice their Speed. At the end of their movement, each enemy within a 5-foot emanation takes 2d6+5 slashing damage, with a DC 30 basic Reflex save.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/quelaunt":{"lang":["Aklo","(Can't Speak Any Language), Telepathy 100 feet"],"notes":{"saves":"+2 to will saves vs. emotion","speed":"fly"},"focus":1,"flavor":"<p>This three-armed, three-legged monster has no discernible eyes, nose, ears, or mouth, and no visible means of ingesting food. Its limbs are distributed so evenly across its body that it's all but impossible to tell which way the creature is oriented at any given time. Few who witness a quelaunt linger on its alien looks for long though, as the invasion of their minds becomes a more pressing concern, sowing doubt, sorrow, and rage. This monstrosity not only delights in the negative emotions of its prey, but feeds on them, gaining strength and sustenance from their dismay. For the quelaunt, no act is too terrible or cruel to inflict on its victims, since the more a creature suffers, the more the quelaunt feasts.</p>\n<p>Quelaunts are known to associate with other aberrant horrors, including jah-tohls and other creatures associated with the Dominion of the Black. However, the more prevalent theory paints them as more alien—perhaps invasive beings from another dimension of pure thought and feeling—and claims that in their natural state they have no physical bodies at all. Few dare speculate further; the only known autopsy of a quelaunt resulted in the researcher's suicide just days afterward and all the notes were mysteriously destroyed. Whatever secrets there are to be unlocked in the anatomy of these bizarre monsters are apparently important enough to warrant great protection from quelaunts, even after death.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Tremorsense (Imprecise) 60 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Tremorsense allows a monster to feel the vibrations through a solid surface caused by movement. It is an imprecise sense with a limited range (listed in the ability). Tremorsense functions only if the monster is on the same surface as the subject, and only if the subject is moving along (or burrowing through) the surface.</p></p>"},{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+2 to Will Saves vs. Emotion","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Emotional Focus","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The quelaunt can cast the following cleric domain spells as 8th-rank occult innate spells at will without spending Focus Points: Captivating Adoration, Delusional Pride, and Ignite Ambition.</p>"},{"n":"Emotional Frenzy","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The quelaunt casts up to three spells chosen from its at-will innate spells and its emotional focus spells.</p>"},{"n":"Feed on Emotion","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack","emotion","incapacitation","mental"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round;</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The quelaunt feeds on the emotional unrest of a single creature within 30 feet that's under a harmful emotion effect. The target must succeed at a DC 37 Will save or take 4d10 mental damage and be Stunned for 1 round.</p>\n<p>If the target fails its saving throw, the quelaunt regains the same number of Hit Points and regains the action it spent to Feed on Emotion. It can't use the regained action to Feed on Emotion again.</p>"},{"n":"Rapid Strikes","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>The quelaunt makes three melee Strikes, each against a different target within reach. The multiple attack penalty applies to each attack but increases only after all the attacks have been made.</p>"},{"n":"Spiral of Despair","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature fails a saving throw to resist one of the quelaunt's innate spells or emotional focus spells</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> As the quelaunt invades the triggering creature's mind and plants the seeds of negative emotions, it also strips away the target's feelings of hope or positivity. The quelaunt can immediately end a single emotion effect from which the triggering creature is benefiting.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/racid-illito":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Dwarven","Halfling"],"gear":["Bottled Lightning (Greater) (2)","Serpent Dagger","Acid Flask (Moderate)","Alchemist's Fire (Moderate)","Hide Armor","Alchemist Goggles","Alchemist's Toolkit","Formula Book","Blightburn Resin","Wyvern Poison (4)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Potent Poisoner","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Poisons Racid applies use their own saving throw DC or 30, whichever is higher.</p>"},{"n":"Alchemical Formulas","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Acid Flask (Moderate)</p>\n<p>Alchemist's Fire (Moderate)</p>\n<p>Blightburn Resin</p>\n<p>Bottled Lightning (Greater)</p>\n<p>Elixir of Life (Moderate)</p>\n<p>Giant Scorpion Venom</p>\n<p>Mistform Elixir (Greater)</p>\n<p>Wyvern Poison</p>"},{"n":"Drip Poison","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You damage a creature with the <em>serpent dagger</em></p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You poison the creature you hit with dagger venom.</p><hr><p><strong>Dagger Venom</strong> (poison)</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 21 Fortitude</p>\n<p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 4 rounds</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 1d8 poison damage and Enfeebled 1</p>"},{"n":"Pinpoint Poisoner","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When Racid successfully Strikes an Off-Guard creature with a poisoned weapon or exposes an off-guard creature to an inhaled poison, the target takes a –2 circumstance penalty to its initial save against the poison.</p>"},{"n":"Quick Alchemy","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Racid creates a single alchemical item from her formula book (see Alchemical Formulas) or a versatile vial. This item has the infused trait, but it remains potent only until the start of her next turn. With her typical preparations, she can use this ability 7 times per day.</p>"},{"n":"Quick Poison","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Racid draws and applies a dose of poison to a weapon she's holding.</p>"},{"n":"Toxic Splash","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Splash damage dealt by Racid's alchemical bombs is increased to 5.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/rayhnne":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Elven"],"gear":["Boot Knife","Flail (2)","Half Plate","Elixir of Life (Major) (2)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Antimagic Armor","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A spell targets you or includes you in its area</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The armor attempts to counteract the triggering spell with the effect of a 7th-rank Dispel Magic spell and a counteract modifier of +26.</p>"},{"n":"Cushioned Blow","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Rayhnne is critically hit with a Strike or spell attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Rayhnne attempts a DC 11 Flat. On a success, the attack becomes a normal hit instead.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Guardbreaker","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Rayhnne makes a Strike against a creature, then Strides. This Stride doesn't trigger reactions. If she ends this Stride in a difference space adjacent to the same creature, she makes another Strike against it. If both Strikes succeed, the creature is Off-Guard until the start of Rayhnne's next turn. Each attack counts against Rayhnne's multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn't increase until she's made both attacks.</p>"},{"n":"Smashing Wave","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p>Rayhnne smashes her flails together, creating a localized shock wave. She chooses whether this effect is a 15-foot emanation or a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area takes 10d6 sonic damage with a DC 34 basic Reflex saving throw. A creature that fails its save is also Dazzled for 1 round. A creature that critically fails is also Deafened for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Spinning Shield","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Rayhnne spins her flails rapidly in all directions, giving her a +2 circumstance bonus to her AC and Reflex saves until the start of her next turn. If she uses Reactive Strike while this ability is active, she adds 1d10 to her damage.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/red-tinged-doorway":{"description":"<p>A swirling portal leads to unwholesome places.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 35 Arcana, DC 35 Occultism, or DC 35 Thievery (master); must have studied Carlina's notes</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(to predict the portal's dangerous destinations)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Warping Journey","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature passes through the doorway</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The creature is pulled apart and reassembled as they pass through multiple dimensions at once. The creature must attempt a DC 30 Will save and disappears for a number of rounds, reappearing at the end of their turn on the final round. Each round at the beginning of their turn, creatures trapped in the doorway must succeed at a DC 32 Fortitude save against a Cursed Metamorphosis spell as their bodies are warped and rearranged. A creature can pass through each red-tinged doorway only once.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature disappears for 1 round. Additionally, the creature gains 10 temporary Hit Points for 24 hours. These stack with temporary Hit Points gained from other red-tinged doorways and replenish each day at midnight as long as the creature is within 1 mile of Narona.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature disappears for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature disappears for 2 rounds.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature disappears for 3 rounds. If the creature critically fails its saving throw against a <em>cursed metamorphosis</em> spell, it's permanently transformed into an amalgamite.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/reynard-hawk":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Sailing Lore",26]],"gear":["Greataxe","Hand Crossbow","Studded Leather Armor","Hellfire Boots","Bolts (20)"],"flavor":"<p>Some hunters grow bored of simple beasts and monsters. For them, a battle-tested warrior is the finest prey.</p><hr><p>Villains pursue selfish and cruel goals, trampling over anyone in their way.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Prepared Trapper","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A hero hunter carries the materials to Craft two Alarm Snares, two Grasping Snares, one Snagging Hook Snare, and one Stunning Snare. The hero hunter replenishes any used supplies each time they make their daily preparations.</p>"},{"n":"Nimble Dodge","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The hero hunter is targeted with a melee or ranged attack by an attacker they can see</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The hero hunter gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Deadly Snares","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The hero hunter Crafts a snare that would normally take 1 minute or less to Craft. The Stealth DC to locate the snare and DC to disable it with Thievery are equal to the hero hunter's Crafting DC if it's higher than the snare's DC.</p>"},{"n":"Devil's Dance","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"once per minute","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per minute</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You Stride. Each square you move through during your Stride is scorched with hellish flames, becoming hazardous terrain for 1 minute. A creature that moves through one of these spaces takes 3d6 fire damage.</p>"},{"n":"Felling Shot","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hero hunter makes a ranged Strike. If it hits and deals damage to a flying target, the target falls up to 120 feet but takes no damage from the fall. The creature can't Fly, Leap, levitate or otherwise leave the ground until the end of the hero hunter's next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Hunter's Precision","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["stance"],"f":"","d":"<p>The hero hunter knows how to hunt and kill any game. While in this stance, all the hero hunter's Strikes deal an additional 2d8 precision damage, and the range increment for their ranged weapon Strikes is 20 feet longer than normal. If the hunter gets a critical hit with a weapon Strike, the target also takes 2d6 persistent bleed damage.</p>"},{"n":"Infernal Jig","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The <em>Sea Mantis</em> is immune to the flames created by Reynard when he activates his <em>hellfire boots</em>.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/rotrovio":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"lore":[["Hell Lore",25]],"gear":["General's Word","Breastplate","Religious Symbol of Asmodeus"],"abilities":[{"n":"Call of Asmodeus","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["divine"],"f":"3 times per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> three times per day</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> A troop within sight of Rotrovio loses a segment</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Rotrovio reanimates the recently slain to rise and fight again. Rotrovio casts Rouse Skeletons as a 5th-rank innate divine spell (Pathfinder Player Core 2 250), including at least one square the lost troop segment previously occupied in the initial area of effect. The triggering troop gains a +4 circumstance bonus to its saves against this spell.</p>"},{"n":"Battlefield Broadcast","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","linguistic","manipulate","mental","occult"],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The weapon amplifies your force of personality across the battlefield with the effects of Telepathy for 10 minutes, except the range is 500 feet. The effect ends immediately if you drop your weapon.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/sedacthy-warband":{"lang":["Thalassic","Sea Speech"],"abilities":[{"n":"Sea Speech","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A sedacthy speaking Thalassic can be understood by any animal that has a swim Speed or the amphibious or aquatic trait. By spending a week regularly interacting with such an animal, the sedacthy can make it permanently helpful.</p>"},{"n":"Wavesense (Imprecise) 30 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>This sense allows a monster to feel vibrations caused by movement through a liquid. It's an imprecise sense with a limited range (listed in the ability). Wavesense functions only if monster and the subject are in the same body of liquid, and only if the subject is moving through the liquid.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Frenzied Feast","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The warband launches a frenzy of attacks against each enemy in a 5-foot emanation with a DC 26 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions. For each enemy damaged by this attack, the damage of the attack increases by 1d4 piercing for all targets (up to a maximum of 3d4 additional damage).</p>\n<p>1 1d6+3 piercing damage plus 1d4 persistent bleed damage</p>\n<p>2 2d6+6 piercing damage plus 1d6 persistent bleed damage</p>\n<p>3 3d6+9 piercing damage plus 1d8 persistent bleed damage</p>"},{"n":"War Shriek","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The warband unleashes a chorus of terrifying battle cries. Each enemy in a 30-foot emanation must attempt a DC 29 Will save. Regardless of the results, creatures are temporarily immune for 1 minute.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Immobilized for 1 round and Frightened 3.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/sigil-of-deepest-fear":{"description":"<p>An arcane sigil forces creatures to confront their greatest fear.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 43 Thievery (master) to drain the sigil's power harmlessly, or Dispel Magic (9th rank; counteract DC 42) to counteract the sigil</p>","reset":"<p>1 day</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Face Your Fear","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["arcane","death","emotion","fear","illusion","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature moves within 10 feet of the sigil</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> All creatures within 120 feet of the sigil are affected by a Phantasmagoria spell (DC 40 Will save).</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/smoking-chimney":{"description":"<p>Smoke billows out from the chimney and fills the room.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 40 Athletics (expert) to pull the blockage from the chimney, DC 46 Thievery (master) to clear the chimney by removing a crucial object and cause everything to fall out, or create water (or similar effect) to extinguish the fire</p>","reset":"<p>The smoking chimney resets when 10 Bulk of objects are placed in it.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action; inhaled, poison) The smoking chimney billows out smoke. If the door from area <strong>A6</strong> is open, the smoke expands 5 feet into the corridor. All creatures in the smoke take 11d6 poison damage (DC 43 basic Fortitude save). On a failure, the target becomes Sickened 1 for 1 round.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Choking Smoke","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["inhaled","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature other than Ivirno enters area <strong>A6</strong></p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Smoke fills the room, concealing all creatures within area <strong>A6</strong>. All creatures in the area other than Ivirno take 11d6 poison damage (DC 43 basic Fortitude save), then the smoking chimney rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/soul-ripper":{"description":"<p>Two hosts of shadowy spirits emerge from Hell to rip Oourax's soul in two, damaging all those who stand in their path.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 33 Diplomacy or DC 33 Deception to convince the spirits to ignore you, or DC 30 Occultism or DC 30 Religion to weaken the haunt; four successes are required to disable it. After 5 rounds, Oourax's soul is sundered and the haunt ends.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action) Oourax's soul attempts to flee, moving 20 feet in a random direction. Her soul is pursued by two hosts of devilish spirits. Large or smaller creatures (or troops composed of Large or smaller creatures) within a 20-foot emanation of Oourax's soul are trampled by the spirits (2d10+13 spirit damage with a DC 28 basic Reflex save).</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Devil's Due","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Oourax dies</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Oourax's soul rises from her body. The haunt rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/special-forces-unit":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Warfare Lore",28]],"notes":{"speed":"troop movement"},"abilities":[{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Short Salvo","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The special forces unit draws and fires a barrage of arrows from their shortbows. The salvo is a 10-foot burst within 60 feet that deals 5d8 piercing damage (DC 34 basic Reflex save). When the special forces unit is reduced to 2 segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Slashing Blades","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p>1 to 3</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The special forces unit attacks each enemy in a 5-foot emanation with its various blades, with a DC 34 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 3d6+2 slashing damage</p>\n<p>2 5d6+7 slashing damage</p>\n<p>3 8d6+10 slashing damage</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/steaming-flow":{"description":"<p>The elemental-infused fountain spouts boiling water in a singular direction, carrying all non-aquatic creatures caught in it across the hallway and toward the perilous drop-off in the opposite tower!</p>","disable":"<p>DC 25 Arcana (trained), DC 25 Nature (trained), or DC 25 Survival (trained) to divert the flow into weaker streams, or DC 27 Athletics, DC 27 Crafting (trained), or DC 27 Thievery (trained) to break up the ground to weaken the flow; two successes (or one critical success) are needed to disable the hazard.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action) The hazard attempts an Athletics check with a +28 modifier to Shove all creatures in the water-filled areas in areas <strong>E5</strong> and <strong>E6</strong> toward the drop-off in area <strong>E7</strong>; the boiling spring gains a +4 circumstance bonus to its Fortitude DC against this effect. Any creature ending its turn in the flow also takes 2d12+12 fire damage with a DC 29 basic Fortitude save.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(expert)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Babbling Brook","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The boiling spring rolls initiative</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The steaming flow rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/storm-tossed-sea":{"description":"<p>A relentless storm assails the ship, battering those on board who don't secure themselves.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 29 Athletics, Crafting, or Sailing Lore to securely lash one's self to the ship. Creatures tied to the ship are immune to the hazard's routine but are Immobilized.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action) The storm tosses the ship in a random direction (roll 1d8 to determine). All creatures on the ship that aren't lashed to it are moved 10 feet in that direction and must attempt a DC 30 Reflex save or Sailing Lore check as the waves pummel them.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature takes no damage and can avoid being moved 10 feet if it wishes.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes no damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Off-Guard and takes 1d12+15 bludgeoning damage.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Prone and takes 2d12+15 bludgeoning damage.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Storm Surge","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The storm builds for at least 10 minutes</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ship pitches dangerously atop the waves. The hazard rolls initiative and performs its routine as a free action.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/stygian-serpent":{"flavor":"<p>These fabled beasts resemble massive snakes with long rows of finned spines down their back. Temperamental and territorial, sea serpents can capsize a boat with ease, and most won't hesitate to do so when hungry or threatened. Stories abound of aggrieved captains who spend their entire lives hunting down the elusive monster that sunk their ships and took their livelihoods. These hunts rely on rumors and glimpses of the beasts, as few survive the catastrophes wrought by sea serpents.</p>\n<p>While many fishermen's tales paint sea serpents as divinely appointed guardians of the ocean or as evil and demonic agents, the truth is that most sea serpents are simply very large beasts with a knack for avoiding magical detection.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Undetectable","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>A sea serpent automatically tries to counteract any detection, revelation, or scrying divination attempted against it, using its Stealth modifier for its counteract modifier.</p>"},{"n":"Stygian","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The serpent is immune to effects of the River Styx.</p>"},{"n":"Capsize","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>The sea serpent attempts to capsize an aquatic vessel of its size or smaller that it's adjacent to. It must succeed at an DC 35 Athletics check with a DC of 35 (reduced by 5 for each size smaller than the sea serpent) or the pilot's Sailing Lore DC, whichever is higher.</p>"},{"n":"Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>1d10+14 bludgeoning, DC 32 basic Fortitude</p>\n<hr>\n<p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC.</p></p>"},{"n":"Sea Serpent Algae","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["incapacitation","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>The water in the ballast organs around the sea serpent's neck is full of psychotropic algae.</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 34 Fortitude</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Confused and, if flying, spends its first action each turn to descend 20 feet (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> confused and, if flying, descends until reaching the ground or water below (1 round)</p>"},{"n":"Spine Rake","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["attack","move"],"f":"","d":"<p>The sea serpent extends the spines along its back and Swims or Strides. Each creature the serpent is adjacent to at any point during its movement takes 4d6+8 slashing damage (DC 32 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Swallow Whole","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>Huge, 2d10+6 bludgeoning, Rupture 20</p>\n<hr>\n<p><p>The monster attempts to swallow a creature of the listed size or smaller that it has grabbed or restrained in its jaws or mouth. If a swallowed creature is of the maximum size listed, the monster can't use Swallow Whole again. If the creature is smaller than the maximum, the monster can usually swallow more creatures; the GM determines the maximum. The monster attempts an Athletics vs. Reflex DC check opposed by the grabbed creature's Reflex DC. If it succeeds, it swallows the creature. The monster's mouth or jaws no longer grab a creature it has swallowed, so the monster is free to use them to Strike or Grab once again. The monster can't attack creatures it has swallowed.</p>\n<p>A swallowed creature is Grabbed, is Slowed 1, and has to hold its breath or start suffocating. The swallowed creature takes the listed amount of damage when first swallowed and at the end of each of its turns while it's swallowed. If the victim Escapes this ability's grabbed condition, it exits through the monster's mouth. This frees any other creature grabbed in the monster's mouth or jaws. A swallowed creature can attack the monster that has swallowed it, but only with unarmed attacks or with weapons of light Bulk or less. The swallowing creature is Off-Guard against the attack. If the monster takes piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding the listed Rupture value from a single attack or spell, the swallowed creature cuts itself free. A creature that gets free by either Escaping or cutting itself free can immediately breathe and exits the swallowing monster's space.</p>\n<p>Effect: Engulf and Swallow Whole</p>\n<p>If the monster dies, a swallowed creature can be freed by creatures adjacent to the corpse if they spend a combined total of 3 actions cutting the monster open with a weapon or unarmed attack that deals piercing or slashing damage.</p></p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/talmandor":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Empyrean","Sussuran","speak with animals, truespeech"],"gear":["Spear"],"abilities":[{"n":"At-Will Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster can cast its at-will spells any number of times without using up spell slots.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Captor's Bane","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["holy"],"f":"","d":"<p>Talmandor's Strikes deal an additional 2d8 spirit damage against any creature that has hindered another creature—by imposing a penalty to a creature's Speed or imposing the clumsy, Grabbed, Immobilized, Paralyzed, or Restrained conditions (including using an action to extend the duration of a grab) to another creature—since the beginning of Talmandor's last turn. One ally hindered by the target can attempt to break free of one of the hindering effects; they can either attempt a new save against the effect that allows a save or attempt to Escape from the effect as a free action.</p>"},{"n":"Coruscating Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["air","holy","light","spirit"],"f":"","d":"<p>Talmandor briefly transforms into a luminous cloud, which doubles his resistance to physical damage, grants him immunity to precision damage, and allows him to move through most creatures and tiny cracks. He then Flies his Speed before returning to his solid form.</p>\n<p>A burst of searing radiance surrounds Talmandor in a 20-foot burst either before or after he becomes a cloud. Each enemy in the area must succeed at a DC 46 Reflex save or take 2d8 persistent spirit damage and be Dazzled until the persistent spirit damage ends. Unholy creatures that fail their save are Blinded for 1 round, after which they're dazzled for the persistent damage's duration.</p>\n<p>Once Talmandor uses this ability, he can't do so again for 1d6 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Twin-Talon Swipe","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["flourish"],"f":"","d":"<p>Talmandor makes two claw Strikes, targeting either the same foe or two adjacent targets. Each attack uses Talmandor's current multiple attack penalty. If they both hit the same target, he combines both Strikes' damage and applies resistances and weaknesses only once.</p>"},{"n":"Zephyr Strikes","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When Talmandor scores a critical hit with a weapon or unarmed Strike, he can Fly or Stride up to 10 feet without triggering reactions.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/tareth-ivici":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"lore":[["Legal Lore",33],["Scribe Lore",30]],"gear":["Staff of Office","Masquerade Scarf (Greater)","Wand of Alarm (Rank 3)"],"notes":{"saves":"+2 circumstance to all saves vs. fear","per":"(+33 to Sense Motive)"},"flavor":"<p>The infernal registrar is a mortal representative of Hell's bureaucracy. They can access copies of all infernal contracts signed by a denizen of their world and can navigate the machinations of Hell's many devils. They can grant special access—for a price.</p><hr><p>Larger societies rely on those with the authority and the ability to interpret and enforce laws. Some carry out these duties fairly, but others are harsh and cruel, imposing severe punishments on anyone unable to pay for clemency.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"+14 to Sense Motive","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Contract Specialist","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>For encounters involving matters of contracts and dealings with Hell, the infernal registrar is an 18th-level challenge.</p>"},{"n":"Death is a Promotion","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The infernal registrar does not fear death, as they have a signed infernal contract for immediate promotion to a mid-ranked devil upon their soul's arrival in Hell. They're immune to all Intimidation checks to Coerce involving threats of death.</p>"},{"n":"Friends in Low Places","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Though devils do not respect most mortals, they respect the office of infernal registrar. No creature with the devil trait of 18th level or lower will knowingly and willingly attack an infernal registrar.</p>"},{"n":"Technically Correct","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The infernal registrar uses their Legal Lore modifier on all Deception checks to Lie.</p>"},{"n":"+2 Circumstance to All Saves vs. Fear","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Masquerade","a":"2","c":"defensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>You arrange the scarf over your lower face, and it casts a 2nd-rank Illusory Disguise spell on you, which ends immediately if the scarf is removed. You can alter the scarf's appearance or make it invisible as part of the <em>illusory disguise</em>, but it can still be felt if touched.</p>"},{"n":"A Favor for a Favor","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The infernal registrar has the authority to make limited infernal contracts with other mortals. They summon a contract with the legal language they desire. Detecting Hidden clauses in the contract requires a successful DC 43 Society or a DC 38 Legal lore check. Once signed, the contract vanishes into the infernal filing system in Hell. The infernal registrar cannot grant any boons beyond their own personal power (usually limited to information, advice, or access to elements of the infernal bureaucracy).</p>"},{"n":"Request Document","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The infernal registrar makes a request to summon a copy of any infernal contract a specific creature has signed. They must know enough information to specifically identify the individual who signed. The infernal registrar attempts a Legal lore check with a DC equal to a hard DC of the level of the creature in question. The infernal registrar will never promise a successful use of this ability in the agreements they make. Each agreement is typically for one attempt. Any copy summoned is simply a copy, has no impact on the original contract if destroyed or altered, and will vanish if taken more than 20 feet from the infernal registrar.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> A copy of the contract appears before the infernal registrar after 10 minutes.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> A copy of the contract appears before the infernal registrar after 1 hour.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The attempt fails, but the infernal registrar can try again after 24 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The attempt fails, and the infernal registrar can't try again for the named creature for 1 year.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/the-foresworn":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Necril"],"lore":[["Hellknight Lore",22]],"gear":["Composite Shortbow","War Flail","Full Plate","Arrows (20)"],"notes":{"hp":"(rejuvenation, void healing)"},"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Rejuvenation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a graveknight is destroyed, their armor rebuilds their body over the course of 1d10 days—or more quickly if the armor is worn by a living host. If the body is destroyed before then, the process restarts.</p>\n<p>A graveknight can only be permanently destroyed by obliterating their armor (such as with Disintegrate), transporting it to the Forge of Creation, or throwing it into the heart of a volcano.</p>"},{"n":"Sacrilegious Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet.</p>\n<p>When a creature in the aura uses a vitality spell or ability, the graveknight automatically attempts to counteract it, with a counteract modifier of +22.</p>"},{"n":"Thorned Armor","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature grapples the Foresworn or Strikes him with an unarmed or melee weapon without the reach trait</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Barbs tangle the triggering creature's attacking limb, and it must attempt a DC 30 Reflex save. On a failure, it must attempt a DC 5 Flat to move away from the Foresworn. On a critical failure, this flat check increases to DC 10.</p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Devastating Blast","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","electricity"],"f":"","d":"<p>The graveknight unleashes a 30-foot cone of energy. Creatures in the area take 20d4 electricity for a creature of the graveknight's level with a DC 33 basic Reflex.</p>\n<p>The graveknight can use this ability once every 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Graveknight's Curse","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["arcane","curse"],"f":"","d":"<p>This curse affects anyone who wears a graveknight's armor for at least 1 hour</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 37 Will save</p>\n<p><strong>Onset</strong> 1 hour</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Doomed 1 and can't remove armor (1 day)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Doomed 2, –10-foot status penalty to Speeds, and can't remove armor (1 day)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> dies and transforms into the armor's graveknight.</p>"},{"n":"Phantom Mount","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","summon"],"f":"","d":"<p>HP 78; AC 30, Fort +22, Ref +16, Will +19</p><hr><p>The graveknight summons a supernatural mount, as Marvelous Mount heightened to a rank equal to half the graveknight's level. Unlike <em>marvelous mount</em>, the steed's AC and saving throw bonuses are all 4 lower than the graveknight's, and the steed has one-third the graveknight's Hit Points (rounded down).</p>\n<p>If the steed is destroyed, the graveknight must wait 1 hour before using this ability again.</p>"},{"n":"Weapon Master","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The graveknight has access to the critical specialization effects of any weapons it wields.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/thephrol":{"lang":["Common","Cyclops","Jotun"],"lore":[["Any One Lore",18]],"gear":["Greatclub","Hide Armor"],"flavor":"<p>Gigantic loners, the great cyclopes are their lesser kin writ large. They're stronger and more violent, but their uncontrolled vision of possible futures has driven them beyond reason. They see every moment as a potential storm of uncontrollable fury and, out of a desperate desire for peace, quiet, and an end to their hunger, lash out at any who come near. Wise creatures avoid great cyclopes at all cost. It's fortunate for humanoids that great cyclopes prefer to dwell far from settlements.</p>\n<p>Debate has long raged over the origins of these massive, destructive giants. They are so large that it had long been assumed they were used as beasts of burden by their lesser kin, now free to hunt and kill without restraint. Other scholars believe the great cyclops is the ultimate fate of the entire cyclops species. Whatever foolish decision or wayward curse caused the end of their civilization is still playing out, occasionally causing a cyclops to withdraw from their own kind, lose all semblance of intellect, and mutate into a lumbering, feral colossus.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>The cyclopes are violent giants with a tragic past. Although they possess only one eye, they could once see far more than most, possessing occult wisdom and divinatory magic that gave them the mystic ability of foresight. But their legendary oracular powers failed to prevent the fall of their society, and the vast kingdoms of the cyclops long ago collapsed into ruin. Today, cyclopes have forgotten much of what they once knew, and they skulk among the crumbling remains of their fallen cities like forgotten kings and queens of their own fallen kingdoms.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Displace","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The amalgamite is hit by a Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The amalgamite Repositions itself or Transposes itself with another creature. If the amalgamite successfully Transposes its location, it and any transposed creature take half damage from the triggering Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Ferocity","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster is reduced to 0 HP.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster avoids being knocked out and remains at 1 HP, but its Wounded value increases by 1. When it is Wounded 3, it can no longer use this ability</p></p>"},{"n":"Flash of Brutality","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":["fortune","occult"],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day, and recharges when the great cyclops uses Ferocity.</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The great cyclops succeeds at an attack roll.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The attack becomes a critical success.</p>"},{"n":"Powerful Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The great cyclops Strides twice and makes a horn Strike. If it moved at least 20 feet away from its starting position, the Strike's damage is increased to 3d10+20.</p>"},{"n":"Reposition","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>The amalgamite teleports into an unoccupied space it can see within 50 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Throw Rock","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster picks up a rock within reach or retrieves a stowed rock and throws it, making a ranged Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Transpose","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>The amalgamite chooses up to two destabilized creatures it can see within 50 feet and swaps their positions, or moves one such creature to an unoccupied space it can see within range. If the amalgamite chooses two creatures, it can choose itself as a target, but both targets must be the same size. An unwilling creature can attempt a DC 33 Will save. If either target succeeds at this saving throw, both are unaffected.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/thin-wisps-fireworks-show":{"description":"<p>Fashionable performers and revolutionaries rappel from the surrounding buildings on scarves.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 21 Acrobatics to turn away from the explosions, or DC 25 Crafting to identify the exact moment the fireworks will explode</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action; visual) The Thin Wisps continue to launch fireworks until the dottari excruciator divisions are defeated. Each round, all creatures must succeed at a DC 24 Fortitude save or be Dazzled and Deafened for 1 round (or Blinded and deafened for 1 round on a critical failure).</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Let the Sparks Fly","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["visual"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A non-dottari creature takes damage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Thin Wisps fire off a series of fireworks as they rappel from the eaves on scarves. All creatures in area A must attempt a DC 24 Fortitude save. On a failure, the target is Dazzled and Deafened until the end of its next turn (or Blinded and deafened on a critical failure). The hazard then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/threshold-kerulkagon":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Empyrean","telepathy 100 feet"],"notes":{"saves":"+2 status to all saves vs. magic"},"flavor":"<p>Kerulkagons are elite, griffon-like guardians specially chosen and transformed by the archdevil Barbatos to interrogate anyone using his plane's myriad portals.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"At-Will Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster can cast its at-will spells any number of times without using up spell slots.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+2 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Anchored Form","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A kerulkagon can't be teleported against its will.</p>"},{"n":"Stand Still","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the kerulkagon's reach uses a move action or leaves a square during a move action it's using</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The kerulkagon makes a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit, the action is disrupted.</p>"},{"n":"Force an Opening","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate","teleportation"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The kerulkagon creates a momentary portal next to a creature within 30 feet and makes a melee Strike through the portal as if the target were within its reach. The target is Off-Guard and gains no cover against the Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Personal Portal","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","teleportation"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The kerulkagon teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 30 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Portal Throw","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack","manipulate","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The kerulkagon has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The kerulkagon creates a portal and attempts to throw the required creature through it. The kerulkagon attempts an Athletics vs. Fortitude DC check against the Fortitude DC of the creature it has grabbed or restrained.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The kerulkagon hurls the target through the portal. The target is teleported violently to a location with 100 feet that the kerulkagon can see, dealing 12d10 bludgeoning damage to the target and knocking it Prone on impact.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> As critical success, but the target takes only 6d10 bludgeoning damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The kerulkagon fails to throw the creature.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature is no longer grabbed or restrained.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/thrune-agent":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"gear":["Dagger (2)","Rapier","Leather Armor","House Thrune Signet Ring"],"abilities":[{"n":"Clever Gambit","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The agent critically hits a creature that they've identified with Recall Knowledge</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The agent Steps or Strides. This movement doesn't trigger reactions from the triggering creature.</p>"},{"n":"Consider Options","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The agent Recalls Knowledge about a creature they can see. On a success, the subject is Off-Guard to the agent until the end of the agent's next turn (or for 1 minute on a critical success).</p>"},{"n":"Debilitating Strike","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The agent's last action was a successful Strike against an Off-Guard creature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Until the end of the agent's next turn, the target takes a –10-foot status penalty to its Speeds or becomes Enfeebled 1. The agent decides which penalty to apply.</p>\n<p>Effect: Debilitating Strike</p>"},{"n":"Deny Advantage","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The agent isn't Off-Guard to hidden, undetected, or flanking creatures of their level or lower, or creatures their level or lower using surprise attack.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The agent deals an additional 3d6 precision damage to creatures that are Off-Guard to them.</p>"},{"n":"Surprise Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the agent rolled Deception or Stealth for initiative, creatures that haven't yet acted are off-guard to them.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/thrune-assassin":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Underworld Lore",16]],"gear":["Composite Shortbow","Rapier","Leather Armor","Darkvision Elixir (Lesser)","Giant Centipede Venom (4)","Invisibility Potion","Lethargy Poison (3)","Arrows (20)","Black Tendril Shot (Lesser)"],"notes":{"speed":"swift sneak"},"flavor":"<p>Assassins commit murder, either for pay or due to their belief in a cause, such as a religion or a political movement. Many are members of assassins' guilds: organizations that accept contracts to kill in return for money, favors, or both.</p><hr><p>In the underbelly of society, the lawless reign supreme.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Swift Sneak","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The assassin can move their full speed when Sneaking.</p>"},{"n":"Deny Advantage","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The assassin isn't Off-Guard to creatures of 8th level or lower that are Hidden, Undetected, flanking or using Surprise Attack.</p>"},{"n":"Nimble Dodge","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The assassin is targeted with a melee or ranged attack by an attacker they can see.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The assassin gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.</p>"},{"n":"Assassin's Poison","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The assassin is wielding a piercing or slashing weapon and has a free hand</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The assassin applies a poison to the weapon. That poison's DC is increased to 26 if it was lower.</p>"},{"n":"Marked for Death","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Each assassin is armed with one lesser black tendril shot that's engraved with the name of a specific PC. If this arrow successfully strikes that PC, the arrow's saving throw and Escape DCs increase by 5, and the save DC against any poison applied to the arrow by their Assassin's Poison ability increases to DC 30</p>"},{"n":"Quick Draw","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The assassin Interacts to draw a weapon, then Strikes with that weapon.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The assassin deals an extra 2d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Surprise Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>On the first round of combat, creatures that haven't acted yet are Off-Guard to the assassin.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/torment-binder":{"lang":["Common","Necril","Shadowtongue"],"lore":[["Spirits Lore",24]],"flavor":"<p>Ghosts and other spirits swirl around the spirit binder, creating a constant aura of flickering faces and forms.</p><hr><p>Hidden secrets and occult powers have an irresistible lure for many. Since the majority of these NPCs are spellcasters, consider using alternative spell lists to adjust their themes.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Spiritsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["detection","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The spirit binder can sense the spirits of creatures, including living creatures, most non-mindless undead, and haunts within the listed range. Since spiritsense detects spiritual essence, not physical bodies, it can detect spirits projected by spells (such as Project Image) or possessing otherwise soulless objects. It can't detect soulless bodies, constructs, or objects, and like most senses, it doesn't penetrate through solid objects.</p>"},{"n":"Haunting Spirits","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","occult","spirit"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. The spirits bound by a spirit binder swirl around, lashing out at their foes. An enemy that enters or starts its turn in the aura must succeed at a DC 27 Will save or take 3d6 spirit damage and be Frightened 1 (double damage and Frightened 2 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Spirit Scrying","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The spirit binder's scrying spells can target or detect spirits on other planes as though the spirits were in the Universe.</p>"},{"n":"Succumb to the Void","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","occult","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>The spirit binder taps into the more nefarious spirits of the Void, becoming something morbid and cruel. For 1d4 rounds, their resistance, aura of spirits, Strikes, and spirit spells change their damage type from spirit damage to void damage and replace their spirit trait with the void trait.</p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Spirit Pitch":"<p>2</p>"}},"hells-destiny-bestiary/ulat-kini-kidnappers":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Military Lore",14]],"notes":{"speed":"troop movement"},"flavor":"<p>Some bands of experienced soldiers have storied reputations, their rolls filled with legendary warriors. Others are whispered of for their cruel deeds and opportunistic betrayals.</p><hr><p>Whether they're hired to wage war, protect a caravan, or infiltrate an impenetrable fortress, there's ample work for mercenaries all over Golarion.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Thresholds</strong> 120 (3 segments), 60 (2 segments)</p>\n<hr>\n<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p>"},{"n":"Claw and Trident","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p>1 to 3</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ulat-kini kidnappers engages in a coordinated attack with its wide array of melee weapons against each enemy in a 5-foot emanation with a DC 25 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 1d8+2 piercing, or slashing</p>\n<p>2 3d8+4 piercing, or slashing</p>\n<p>3 4d8+6 piercing, or slashing</p>"},{"n":"Ready... Fire!","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The ulat-kini kidnappers draws or reloads their bows, crossbows, and slings, then launches a ranged attack in the form of a volley. This volley is a 10-foot burst within 120 feet that deals 2d8+4 piercing or bludgeoning damage with a DC 25 basic Reflex save. When the ulat-kini kidnappers is reduced to 2 or fewer segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p>"},{"n":"Spoils of War","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The kidnappers' last action was Let 'em Have It and at least one creature failed its save</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ulat-kini kidnappers attempts to Steal one object from each enemy that failed its save, even if the enemy is in combat or on guard.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/ulat-kini-scout":{"lang":["Alghollthu","Azlanti","Common"],"gear":["Ranseur"],"abilities":[{"n":"Sea-Beast Rider","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The ulat-kini scout automatically succeeds at checks to Command an Animal with the aquatic trait that their riding. The first attack the ulat-kini makes each round doesn't share a multiple attack penalty with their mount.</p>"},{"n":"Blood in the Water","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The ulat-kini scout begins their turn within 30 feet of a creature taking persistent bleed damage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Until the beginning of their next turn, the ulat-kini gains 9 temporary Hit Points and a +4 status bonus to their Strikes' damage rolls.</p>\n<p>Effect: Blood in the Water</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/urdun-gravelhands":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Halfling","Osiriani"],"lore":[["Favored City Lore",25]],"gear":["Handwraps of Mighty Blows","Sling","Cheap Beer (5)","Darkvision Elixir (Moderate)","Healing Potion (Moderate) (2)","Mistform Elixir (Moderate)","Sling Bullets (20)","Freezing Sling Bullets (5)"],"notes":{"saves":"+2 vs. poison"},"abilities":[{"n":"Deep Cover Specialist","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>For matters relating to spycraft and undercover operations, Urdun Gravelhands is a 14th-level challenge.</p>"},{"n":"Favored City","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Urdun can establish a settlement of at least 5,000 people as his favored city by spending 1 week exploring and making contacts there. He can use his Favored City Lore skill to Recall Knowledge about the city; he gains a +4 circumstance bonus to his Deception and Stealth checks while in his favored city; and he applies abilities like city shepherd to his allies while in his favored city. Urdun can have only one favored city at a time (Corentyn, at the beginning of this adventure), replacing his prior settlement whenever he establishes a new favored city.</p>"},{"n":"+2 Status to All Saves vs. Poison","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"City Shepherd","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>While in his favored city, all allies who can observe Urdun can add their level + 2 as their proficiency bonus when attempting Deception or Stealth checks, as if Following the Expert.</p>"},{"n":"Fighting Drink","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Urdun rolls Initiative</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> He consumes a dose of alcohol and begins his Soused Ruse as a free action. He rolls Deception for Initiative. Creatures that haven't acted yet are Off-Guard to him.</p>"},{"n":"Soused Ruse","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Urdun consumes a dose of alcohol</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> He appears to become drunk (the same as succumbing to stage 1 of alcohol's poison) without suffering from the condition, and he gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Deception checks to Feint against creatures that assume he's intoxicated. A creature can identify his ruse either by Sensing Motive or by succeeding at a Medicine check against his Deception DC while observing him within 30 feet.</p>\n<p>Effect: Soused Ruse</p>"},{"n":"Break Bottle","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Urdun shatters a bottle and uses it to brawl. For the next 1 minute when he makes a fist Strike, he can choose for the Strike to lose the unarmed trait, gain the versatile P trait, and deal 1d6 persistent bleed damage on critical hits.</p>"},{"n":"Ruse Drinker","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>Urdun Draws and Activates a consumable item he can drink, such as a potion, elixir, or alcoholic drink.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Urdun's Strikes deal an additional 2d6 precision damage against Off-Guard creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Sobering Stride","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["move"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Urdun's Soused Ruse is active</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Urdun pretends to sober up as he moves more quickly. He Strides twice and ends his Soused Ruse.</p>"},{"n":"Soused Blow","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["flourish"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Urdun's Soused Ruse is active</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Urdun pretends to stumble while preparing a punch. He Feints then makes a melee Strike.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/uro-adom":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic"],"lore":[["Hellknight Lore",22]],"gear":["Longsword","Sturdy Shield (Lesser)","Hellknight Plate","10-foot Length of Chain (4)","Manacles (Good) (4)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Roaring Initiative","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Uro rolls Intimidation for initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Hell-Bound Guard","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Uro rolls initiative</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> His hell-bound guard (an elite warden devil) appears and fights to protect him.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Chain Choke","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Uro has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Uro uses a length of chain to choke his target. The target takes 2d6+11 bludgeoning damage (DC 29 basic Fortitude save). On a failure, the target must begin holding its breath. On a critical failure, the target falls Unconscious and starts suffocating.</p>"},{"n":"Manacled Grab","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When Uro critically hits with a longsword Strike, he can apply manacles as part of his Improved Grab. If a creature would fail an attempt to Escape his Grab, it critically fails instead.</p>"},{"n":"Shield Grab","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Uro can use his hand wielding a shield to Grab a creature, though he can't Raise a Shield while grabbing or restraining a creature with his shield arm.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/vanda-spitelash":{"lang":["Common","Empyrean"],"gear":["Crossbow","Longsword","Steel Shield","Full Plate","Religious Symbol of Asmodeus","Potion of Flying (Standard)","Viper's Fang","Bolts (20)"],"focus":2,"flavor":"<p>The deific champion is the paragon of champions, representing the truest form of devotion and dedication to a deity.</p><hr><p>Religions inspire devout individuals to uphold their tenets.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Blessed Shield","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>In the deific champion's hands, a shield gains the <em>moderate reinforcing rune</em>, giving it Hardness 8, 84 HP, and BT 42.</p>"},{"n":"Deific Reactions","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>At the start of each of their turns, the deific champion gains an additional reaction they can only use to make a Reactive Strike or to Shield Block.</p>"},{"n":"Champion's Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>15 feet. Any follower of Asmodeus in the aura knows the champion is a champion of Asmodeus. Enemies in the champion's aura take a –1 circumstance penalty to saving throws against fear. In addition, an enemy that ends its turn in the champion's aura can't reduce the value of its frightened condition below 1.</p>"},{"n":"Champion's Courage","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the champion becomes Frightened, they reduce the condition value by 1 (to a minimum of 0).</p>"},{"n":"Exalted Retributive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy damages the deific champion's ally, and both are in the deific champion's aura</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ally gains resistance 14 to all damage against the triggering damage. If the enemy is within reach, the deific champion makes a melee Strike against it. Each ally in the champion's aura can spend a reaction to Strike the target with a –5 penalty.</p>\n<p>Effect: Exalted Retributive Strike</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Will Not Fall","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The deific champion's Hit Points are reduced to 0 for the first time that day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The champion presses on, refusing to fail their god. They remain standing with 25 Hit Points.</p>"},{"n":"Viper's Fang","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within your reach uses a manipulate or move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a moving action it's using</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You are a master with the affixed weapon</p><hr><p>When you activate this resin-strengthened viper skull, make a melee Strike against the triggering creature.</p>\n<p>If you have Reactive Strike, you can activate the <em>viper's fang</em> as a free action.</p>\n<p>If your attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, you disrupt that action.</p>\n<p>This Strike doesn't count toward your multiple attack penalty, and your multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p><hr><p>If you hit with this attack, the creature is exposed to viper fang venom.</p>\n<p><strong>Viper Fang Venom</strong> (poison)</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 32 Fortitude</p>\n<p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 4 rounds</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 3d10 poison damage and Enfeebled 1.</p>"},{"n":"Will Not Falter","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Effect</strong> The deific champion declares their devotion to their deity and their cause. They Stride, then make a melee Strike. If the Strike hits an enemy, all allies within their champion's aura gain a +2 status bonus to attack rolls and saving throws against fear until the start of the deific champion's next turn.</p>\n<p>Effect: Will Not Falter</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/vicious-levaloch-squad":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Empyrean","telepathy 100 feet"],"lore":[["Warfare Lore",33]],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","per":"(commanded by weak deimavigga or Aspexia Rugatonn for initiative)","speed":"troop movement"},"abilities":[{"n":"Hellstrider","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The levaloch battalion ignores the effects of non-magical difficult terrain. They take no damage from caltrops or from damaging terrain that deals physical, acid, or cold damage. A levaloch battalion can move through liquids up to 5 feet deep at their full Speed.</p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Troop Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Troops are composed of many individuals, represented by four \"segments\" on a battle grid. Each segment is 10 feet on each side and as tall as the individual members of the troop. Segments must remain contiguous. Each one has to share at least 5 feet of one of its edges with another segment—being adjacent on a diagonal isn't sufficient! You can measure flanking, cover, and the like using the center of any segment.</p>\n<p>A troop has two Hit Point thresholds in its HP entry and loses segments as it crosses thresholds. Typically, the higher threshold is at 2/3 of the troop's maximum Hit Points and the lower is at 1/3 of its maximum. Once the troop drops below the higher threshold, it loses one segment, leaving three segments (12 squares) remaining and setting the first threshold as the troop's new maximum Hit Points. This repeats when the troop drops below the lower threshold, leaving two segments (8 squares). At 0 Hit Points, the troop disperses entirely, with the few remaining members surrendering, Fleeing, or easily dispatched, as determined by the GM. Typically the creature who caused the troop to lose a segment decides which to remove, or the GM decides when a specific creature wasn't responsible. To restore lost segments and maximum Hit Points, a troop needs to spend downtime to use long-term treatment on casualties or recruit new members to replace the fallen.</p>\n<p>Troops are typically immune to non-damaging effects that target a single creature, such as a Charm spell or the Demoralize action. An ability that can target 5 or more creatures can target an entire segment, increasing to two segments if it can target 10 or more creatures and to the entire troop if it can target 20 or more creatures. An ability that affects all creatures in a certain range affects all segments in range (make any checks or saves separately for each segment). As examples, an 8th rank <em>charm</em> spell (with 10 targets) can affect two segments, and an ability that Demoralizes all creatures within 30 feet of you would affect all segments that are fully within that range. A non-damaging ability that would prevent a segment from acting, cause them to flee, or otherwise make them unable to function as part of the troop for a round or more removes the segment entirely. The troop loses a number of HP required to bring it to the next threshold. If an ability both deals damage and has a non-damaging effect, apply the damage then the rest of the effect.</p></p>"},{"n":"Troop Movement","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>Whenever a troop moves, you move one of its segments and the other segments follow behind it. At the end of the movement, you can group the other segments adjacent to the one you moved as you see fit, provided none of them moves farther than the moving segment. If you choose not to move the troop any distance, you can instead reshape the position of all the segments as long as one stays in place.</p></p>"},{"n":"Barbed Net Barrage","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["magical","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>The battalion hurls barbed nets. This barrage is a 10-foot burst within 30 feet that deals 6d8 slashing damage with a DC 37 Reflex save. A creature can Escape from the penalties imposed by these nets, but each Escape attempt deals 3d6 slashing damage to the creature from the nets' barbs, regardless of whether the attempt succeeds. When the levaloch battalion is reduced to 2 segments, this area decreases to a 5-foot burst.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature takes no damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage and takes a –5-foot circumstance penalty to its Speeds until it Escapes.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage, is Clumsy 1, and takes a –10-foot circumstance penalty to its Speeds until it Escapes.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage, is Clumsy 2, and is Immobilized until it Escapes.</p>"},{"n":"Merciless Tridents","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["magical","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>The levalochs make coordinated melee attacks with their tridents. Each enemy within a 5-foot emanation must attempt a DC 37 basic Reflex save. The damage depends on the number of actions.</p>\n<p>1 2d8 piercing damage plus vicious cruelty</p>\n<p>2 4d8+10 piercing damage plus vicious cruelty</p>\n<p>3 6d8+12 piercing damage plus vicious cruelty</p>"},{"n":"Vicious Cruelty","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature that has the clumsy, enfeebled, Immobilized, or Restrained condition takes an additional 1d6 precision damage from Merciless Tridents (2d6 precision damage if the levalochs take 2 or 3 actions).</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/vinculatti":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Empyrean","telepathy 100 feet"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","per":"fearsense (precise) 60 feet"},"flavor":"<p>Warden devils exist to capture and imprison mortals, whether as jailers in Hell or hunters summoned by diabolists. Vinculattis exercise little discretion and show less interest in a prisoner's sentence or condition. Warden devils take cruel satisfaction in heaping psychological distress on their charges, enumerating the pleasures a prisoner is now denied.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"Fearsense 60 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The vinculatti is aware of all frightened creatures within the listed range.</p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Jingling Approach","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a creature rolls Perception for its initiative in combat against the vinculatti or succeeds at a Perception check against the vinculatti's Stealth DC, it must attempt a DC 27 Will save. On a failure, it's Frightened 1 (Frightened 2 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"No Liberation","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature Grabbed or Restrained by the vinculatti attempts to Escape</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The triggering creature takes a –2 circumstance penalty to the check to Escape.</p>"},{"n":"Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>1d12+13 bludgeoning, DC 30 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC.</p></p>"},{"n":"Master of Manacles","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The vinculatti's manacles can grapple or restrain any number of creatures within the devil's reach. They can apply the nonlethal trait to Constrict when damaging foes Grabbed or Restrained by their manacles.</p>"},{"n":"Prisoner Transfer","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> A Large or smaller creature is Grabbed or Restrained by the vinculatti's mandibles</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The vinculatti moves the creature to their manacles, freeing their mandibles to make attacks, and then Constricts the creature it moved.</p>"},{"n":"To the Cells","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The vinculatti Strides or Climbs up to half their Speed, moving any creatures it has Grabbed or Restrained the same distance in that direction.</p>"},{"n":"Whispers of Despair","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> A creature is Grabbed or Restrained by the vinculatti</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The vinculatti taunts the creature about its captivity. The creature must attempt a DC 30 Will save. On a failure, it becomes Frightened 2 (Frightened 3 on a critical failure). Regardless of the save's result, the target is temporarily immune to Whispers of Despair for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/visage-of-asmodeus":{"description":"<p>A looming illusory image of the face of Asmodeus appears within the room, eyes glinting with malice at any who refuse to worship him.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 50 Thievery (master) to disrupt the rune projecting Asmodeus's face or DC 48 Religion (master) to refute the Asmodean faith; four total successes are required to disable the hazard</p>","reset":"<p>The trap deactivates 1 round after all creatures who don't worship Asmodeus either leave the room or are dead. It resets 1 round after that.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action; mental, visual) The illusory face of Asmodeus gazes at one creature in the area who doesn't worship Asmodeus. His eyes glint with diabolic power as that creature is overwhelmed by visions of the enormity of Hell. That creature must attempt a DC 44 Will saving throw. The hazard tends to target creatures who are attempting to disable the hazard. Taking damage from this hazard doesn't grant a flat check to end the Confused condition.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes 5d8 mental damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes 10d8 mental damage and is confused for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes 20d8 mental damage and is confused for 1 minute.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master) to find the face-projecting rune</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Menacing Laughter","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature who doesn't worship Asmodeus enters the room</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The booming voice of Asmodeus laughs cruelly at nonbelievers who would dare enter his highest temple on Golarion. Each creature who doesn't worship Asmodeus within 100 feet must attempt a DC 48 Will save. The hazard then rolls initiative as Asmodeus' face appears in the middle of the vestry.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 3 and Slowed 1 for as long as they're frightened.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but Frightened 4.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/vorrea-talminari":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Mwangi"],"lore":[["Sailing Lore",36]],"gear":["Scimitar","Reactive Mail (Major)","Commandant's Scabbard","Fireproof Gloves (Greater)","Magical Medal (Phoenix's Fire)"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. fear"},"abilities":[{"n":"Supple Wrist","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Vorrea Talminari gains an additional reaction each round that can only be used for A Foolish Move.</p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Fear","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"A Foolish Move","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature critically misses Vorrea Talminari with a melee Strike or melee spell attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Vorrea makes an Arcane Strike against the triggering creature using Gouging Claw but becomes Slowed 1 for her next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Focus from Fear","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Though fear weakens Vorrea's other abilities, it hones her offensive abilities. She applies only half her frightened condition value as a penalty to attack rolls (rounded down) and applies a status bonus to damage dealt by her Strikes equal to her frightened value.</p>"},{"n":"Phoenix's Sacrifice","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":["vitality"],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Your Dying condition increases</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The phoenix bursts into flames. You lose the dying condition and regain 1 Hit Point. Your Wounded value does not increase. You can use this action while Unconscious.</p>"},{"n":"Quick Spike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["manipulate","metal"],"f":"once per hour","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 15 feet uses a manipulate action</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> An iron spike launches from your armor at the target, dealing 7d8 piercing damage to the target (DC 36 basic Reflex save). If the target critically fails, the triggering action is disrupted.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Arcane Strike","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Vorrea Talminari Casts a Spell that deals damage. She then makes a melee Strike that counts as two attacks for the purposes of her multiple attack penalty but doesn't apply this penalty until after her Arcane Strike is concluded. If the spell requires an attack roll, use the Strike's results to determine the effects of both the Strike and the spell. If the spell requires a save, the target of the Strike rolls its saving throw normally, though if the Strike was a critical failure, the target is unaffected. Spells used through Arcane Strike can affect only a single target, even if they would normally affect an area or multiple targets.</p>"},{"n":"Commanding Draw","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["fortune"],"f":"once per hour","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You have a weapon sheathed in your Commandant's Scabbard</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You Interact to draw your weapon from your scabbard and Strike with it. On that Strike, you can roll twice and take the better result.</p>\n<p>Effect: Commanding Draw</p>"},{"n":"Fancy Bladework","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>Vorrea attempts an Intimidation check to Demoralize each enemy within 30 feet, without suffering penalties for not sharing a language. Regardless of the result, each creature is temporarily immune to Fancy Bladework for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Paracountess's Parry","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Vorrea Talminari just used Arcane Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Vorrea raises the wide hilt of her cutlass in a defensive posture, surrounded by arcane energies to defend herself. She gains a +2 circumstance bonus to her AC and resistance 5 to physical damage (except silver) until the start of her next turn.</p>\n<p>Effect: Paracountess's Parry</p>"},{"n":"Release Heat","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","fire"],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You have a free hand</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You take the heat that's built up in your gloves and discharge it onto an enemy. You deal 10d8 fire damage to one creature within reach (DC 31 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Steady Spellcasting","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If a reaction would disrupt Vorrea's spellcasting action, she attempts a DC 15 Flat. On a success, her action isn't disrupted.</p>"},{"n":"Wind and Waves","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>Vorrea channels the elemental connection she has with the winds. She teleports to any square within 20 feet that's within reach of a creature, then makes a melee Strike. She can't use Wind and Waves again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/voulgarghas":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Empyrean","telepathy 100 feet, truespeech"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"flavor":"<p>Masters of possession, bdellavritras enact complex schemes through pawns in the mortal world. Even if expelled from their hosts, these fiends retain fearsome physical strength with bodies that bely their agility.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Telepathy 100 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","magical","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A monster with telepathy can communicate mentally with any creatures within the listed radius, as long as they share a language. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts, and communicates no more information than normal speech would.</p></p>"},{"n":"At-Will Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster can cast its at-will spells any number of times without using up spell slots.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>3d8+9 bludgeoning plus 2d6 cold, DC 41 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC.</p></p>"},{"n":"Frosty Whispers","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","cold","emotion","mental"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Voulgarghas sings charming pleasantries from one of their four mouths to a single target within 30 feet. The target takes 10d6 cold damage and must attempt a DC 44 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage and is Stupefied 1 for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage, gains weakness 10 to cold, and is stupefied 1 for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage, gains weakness 15 to cold, and is Stupefied 2 for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Mental Synergy","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","spellshape"],"f":"once per minute","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per minute</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The bdellavritra is possessing a host using Mind Worm</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If the bdellavritra's next action is to Cast a Spell, they reduce the number of actions to cast it by 1 (minimum 1 action).</p>"},{"n":"Mind Worm","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","incapacitation","mental","possession"],"f":"","d":"<p>The bdellavritra spends 10 minutes adjacent to an Unconscious or willing living creature, then attempts to possess its body. This functions as Possession heightened to 9th rank (DC 37 Will save), except that it has a duration of 1 month. If affected, the host receives new saving throws only at the start of each day. If the host dies, the bdellavritra must attempt a Fortitude save as normal but is only Stunned 2 on a failure (or Stunned 4 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/wave-of-damned-souls":{"description":"<p>A torrent of souls pulled from Hell pours through an archway, inflicting their personal suffering on all they touch.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 50 Occultism (master) or DC 50 Religion (master) to quell the souls' suffering; these checks must be attempted while adjacent to the arch, and four total successes are required to disable the haunt</p>","reset":"<p>After 1 minute, the wave of souls dries up, and the haunt deactivates. Over the course of 1 hour, planar energy rebuilds in the area, and the haunt resets.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action; divine, void) A seemingly endless flow of damned spirits emerges from the arch and washes down the street. Each creature within a 240-foot line from the arch down the street takes 4d10+24 void damage with a DC 44 Fortitude save. This line affects everyone within 20 feet of the ground.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and increases its doomed value by 1.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage and increases its doomed value by 2.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Rising Tide of Screams","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","divine","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A living creature comes within 15 feet of the arch</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The sounds of screams from the damned intensify as the arch begins to glow with planar energy. Each living creature within 60 feet of the arch must attempt a DC 48 Will saving throw. The haunt then rolls initiative.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 3 and can't reduce its frightened condition below 1 for the haunt's duration.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 4 and can't reduce its frightened condition below 2 for the duration of the haunt.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/window-alarm":{"description":"<p>Transparent runes around the window's edge trigger a silent alarm shortly after being opened by an unauthorized person.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 40 Thievery (master) to carefully scuff the faint runes around the window's edge</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(master)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Signal the Keys","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["scrying"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The window is broken or is unlocked and opened without using one of the shop keys</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Each person carrying a shop key within 500 feet receives a mental image of the area 10 feet around the window for 1 minute.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/wretched-diabolist":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Empyrean","Necril"],"lore":[["Hell Lore",41]],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Steady Spellcasting","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If a reaction would disrupt the wretched diabolist's spellcasting action, the diabolist attempts a DC 15 Flat. On a success, the action isn't disrupted.</p>"},{"n":"Wail of the Damned","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","divine","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The diabolist laments their fate; Each living creature within 60 feet must attempt a DC 42 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is temporarily immune to this wretched diabolist's Wail of the Damned for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 3.</p>"}]},"hells-destiny-bestiary/xoxren-killiani":{"lang":["Alghollthu","Azlanti","Common"],"gear":["Dagger","Amulet of the Slumberer","Key","Elixir of Life (Greater) (2)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Vortex","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","water"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet.</p>\n<p>While Xoxren wears the Amulet of the Slumberer, water in the area is difficult terrain for swimming creatures that don't have the water trait.</p>"},{"n":"Consume Sacrifice","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["death","healing","occult"],"f":"once per turn","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per turn</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> A sacrificial victim within 30 feet of Xoxren is tied to a sacrificial pillar</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Xoxren draws the final dregs of life from the victim. He gains 5d8 healing Hit Points and a +2 circumstance bonus to the DCs of his spells until the end of his next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Unleash Tormented Psyche","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Xoxren's turn begins</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Xoxren is in an encounter, he Cast a Spell on his previous turn, and he isn't stupefied</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> While his psyche is unleashed, Xoxren's damaging spells deal an additional 3d6 mental damage to one target or 1d6 mental damage to each target if there are multiple targets. Xoxren's psyche remains unleashed for 2 rounds or until he falls Unconscious. Afterward, he is Stupefied 1 for 2 rounds.</p>"}]}});
